 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L=2: the site-1 rotation on the SoV vacuum as ladder-1 Q-brackets for general reps, [2,1,0] (regression), [3,1,0], [3,2,0] (2026-10-10)\n\nImplements `L2-site1-rotation-brackets-general-spec.md`; generalises `L2-210-site1-rotation-brackets.wb`/`.md`. Setting: companion frame, new conventions, plain GT generators (exact sparse rationals), h = 1/2, theta = (2/7, -3/5) (t = theta12/h = 62/35), twist z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3) (z' = (3/2, 5/4, 3/7) and six more (h, theta) in Task 7), prec = 60 for eigenvectors, dual Q's and SoV covectors; everything else exact.\n\n**One switch.** The only rep-dependent line is `Λ = {2, 1, 0}; nL = 2; ...` in the first code cell after the title (cell 3). The cells below are rep-generic; each result block under a task lists the three reps side by side ([2,1,0] = regression, must reproduce the quadric 43/16 = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) and the adjoint reach table; then [3,1,0], [3,2,0]). The code was run three times, once per rep, by changing that line.\n\n**Notation.** SoV label (a|bc) <-> root triple theta_s + {-1-a, -b, -c} h, sorted triple (m1, m21, m22) = (-1-a, -b, -c); points m = -1-lambda1..0 on ladder s (theta_s + m h); v(x) = (Q^1, Q^2, Q^3)(x) the dual Q's; group c2 = site-2 label (lambda1|lambda1 c2) (c2 = lambda2 is the vacuum), factor lambda2^(c2) = v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h); column c = Q^3 point value at theta1 - c h; Gauss chart g = exp(gA E12) exp(gB E13) exp(gC E23) (alpha, beta, gamma), first row of the 3x3 unipotent b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC), \"genuine\" = gA gB gC != 0. \"0(accN)\" in the printed tables means an exactly-zero-looking bigfloat of accuracy N digits, i.e. a deviation below 10^-N.\n\n**Notebook state.** VS Code did not open/execute cells of this new file (runCell: notebook-not-open). Every code cell was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 from exactly the saved source text (one cell = one `Get`-style evaluation), and the printed results are stored in the markdown cells under the code cells; there are no native outputs. The Task 7 driver (cells near the end) re-reads this notebook's own file to re-run the setup cells with other parameters and must be run LAST (it wipes Global`).\n\n**Section 6b (added 2026-10-10, later session).** Closed-form bracket measures on the loci of [3,1,0] and [2,1,0], their verification, structure, natural-measure test and a cheap t-dependence (cells after the Task 6 results). Like the rest of the notebook these were evaluated in the shared kernel from the saved cell text (VS Code does not open this file); the printed results are in the markdown cells below the code cells.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
