  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. SoV basis and labels, wavefunction monomial (Task 1)\n\nUntwisted L=2 B(u) = T11(u) qmin_{12,12}(u+h) + T21(u) qmin_{12,13}(u+h) (exact sparse, degree 6), left eigenvectors at u = 3/11 (dense, prec 60) = the SoV covectors; eigenvalue polynomial from the largest component at 7 points, six roots per state; a root belongs to ladder s if (root - theta_s)/h is an integer. Label rule tested: sorted triples {-1-a, -b, -c} with lambda2 <= a <= lambda1, 0 <= c <= lambda2, c <= b <= a; vacuum (lambda1|lambda1 lambda2). Wavefunction test: <x_m|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> = N_m prod_s M^(s)_m/M^(s)_vac with M_(a|bc) = det2[v(theta - (1+a)h), v(theta - bh)]_rows v_k(theta - ch), for (rows, k) = ({1,2},1), ({2,3},3), ({1,3},2), all labels x all states, N_m fixed by the state with the largest predicted value.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* untwisted L=2 B(u) = T11(u) qmin_{12,12}(u+h) + T21(u) qmin_{12,13}(u+h) (exact, sparse); its left eigenvectors are the SoV covectors; labels from the six roots of each eigenvalue polynomial *)\nBop2[x_] := mono2[Id3][x][[1, 1]] . qmin[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 2}][x + hN] + mono2[Id3][x][[2, 1]] . qmin[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 3}][x + hN];\n{tims[\"B at 7 points (exact)\"], BnumX} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[Bop2[uPts[[k]]], {k, 7}]];\nBnumN = N[BnumX, prec];\nu0B = 3/11;\n{tims[\"B eigensystem (dense, prec 60)\"], eigB} = AbsoluteTiming[Eigensystem[Transpose[Normal[N[Bop2[u0B], prec]]]]];\n{evB, vecB} = eigB;\ngapB = Min[Abs[Subtract @@@ Subsets[evB, {2}]]];\nrootsOf[cvec_] := Module[{k = Ordering[Abs[cvec], -1][[1]], vals, poly},\n  vals = Table[(cvec . BnumN[[j]])[[k]]/cvec[[k]], {j, 7}];\n  poly = Expand[Sum[vals[[j]] Product[(u - uPts[[l]])/(uPts[[j]] - uPts[[l]]), {l, DeleteCases[Range[7], j]}], {j, 7}]];\n  Sort[Chop[u /. NSolve[poly == 0, u, WorkingPrecision -> 40], 10^-20]]];\n{tims[\"B eigenvalue roots\"], sovRoots} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[rootsOf[cv], {cv, vecB}]];\n(* a root belongs to ladder s if (root - theta_s)/h is an integer *)\nladderOf[r_] := Module[{t1 = (r - thN[[1]])/hN, t2 = (r - thN[[2]])/hN}, Which[Abs[t1 - Round[t1]] < 10^-15, {1, Round[t1]}, Abs[t2 - Round[t2]] < 10^-15, {2, Round[t2]}, True, {0, r}]];\nlab[m_] := lab[m] = {Sort[Map[Last, Select[ladderOf /@ sovRoots[[m]], First[#] == 1 &]]], Sort[Map[Last, Select[ladderOf /@ sovRoots[[m]], First[#] == 2 &]]]};\nlabRule = Flatten[Table[Table[{-1 - a, -b, -c}, {b, c, a}], {a, Λ[[2]], Λ[[1]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2];\nvacTrip = {-1 - Λ[[1]], -Λ[[1]], -Λ[[2]]};\nallLabs = Table[lab[m], {m, nS}];\nchecks[\"B: all roots on the two ladders, 3 + 3\"] = And @@ (Length[#[[1]]] == 3 && Length[#[[2]]] == 3 & /@ allLabs);\nchecks[\"B: rule set size = dim V; label rule: every site triple is {-1-a,-b,-c}, 15 distinct\"] = {Length[labRule], Sort[Union[allLabs[[All, 1]]]] === Sort[labRule] && Sort[Union[allLabs[[All, 2]]]] === Sort[labRule]};\nchecks[\"B: (site-1, site-2) label pairs: # distinct (225 = bijection)\"] = Length[Union[allLabs]];\nchecks[\"B: vacuum triple present on both sites\"] = MemberQ[allLabs, {vacTrip, vacTrip}];\nvacIdx = First[Flatten[Position[allLabs, {vacTrip, vacTrip}]]];\nchecks[\"x0 = e1 tensor e1 is the left eigenvector of B with the vacuum label (exact eigen-test, parallel to vecB[vac])\"] = {Norm[Normal[x0C . Bop2[u0B]] - ((x0C . Bop2[u0B])[[1]]) x0C] === 0, N[1 - Abs[Conjugate[vecB[[vacIdx]]] . x0C]/Norm[x0C], 3]};\nlabTable = Table[{\"(a|bc) = (\" <> ToString[-1 - l[[1]]] <> \"|\" <> ToString[-l[[2]]] <> ToString[-l[[3]]] <> \")\", l}, {l, labRule}];\nGrid[{{\"B eigensystem: gap (min), time (s)\", {N[gapB, 3], tims[\"B eigensystem (dense, prec 60)\"]}}, {\"all roots on ladders 3+3\", checks[\"B: all roots on the two ladders, 3 + 3\"]}, {\"|rule| = dim V; triples = rule set (both sites)\", checks[\"B: rule set size = dim V; label rule: every site triple is {-1-a,-b,-c}, 15 distinct\"]}, {\"# distinct label pairs\", checks[\"B: (site-1, site-2) label pairs: # distinct (225 = bijection)\"]}, {\"vacuum label pair present, index\", {checks[\"B: vacuum triple present on both sites\"], vacIdx}}, {\"label (a|bc) <-> sorted triple of root offsets (theta_s + offset h)\", labTable}, {\"x0 vacuum eigenvector\", checks[\"x0 = e1 tensor e1 is the left eigenvector of B with the vacuum label (exact eigen-test, parallel to vecB[vac])\"]}, {\"times (s): B(7 pts), roots\", {tims[\"B at 7 points (exact)\"], tims[\"B eigenvalue roots\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule. <x_m|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> = N_m prod_s M^(s)_m / (vacuum), M_(a|bc) = det2[v(theta - (1+a)h), v(theta - b h)]_rows . v_k(theta - c h), N_m state independent. All 225 states, three (rows, k) conventions. *)\n{tims[\"SoV overlaps with kets\"], ovlM} = AbsoluteTiming[vecB . Transpose[ketC]];\nratioM = Table[ovlM[[m, A]]/(x0C . ketC[[A]]), {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\nlabIdx[l_] := First[Flatten[Position[labRule, l]]];\nsiteIdx = Table[{labIdx[allLabs[[m, 1]]], labIdx[allLabs[[m, 2]]]}, {m, nS}];\n(* det2[v(m21), v(m1)] v_k(m22) on rows {a,b}: one value per state, site, label *)\nsiteMono[rows_, k_] := Table[Table[With[{m1 = l[[1]], m21 = l[[2]], m22 = l[[3]]}, (vm[A, s, m21][[rows[[1]]]] vm[A, s, m1][[rows[[2]]]] - vm[A, s, m21][[rows[[2]]]] vm[A, s, m1][[rows[[1]]]]) vm[A, s, m22][[k]]], {l, labRule}], {A, nS}, {s, nL}];\nwfTest[rows_, k_] := Module[{sm = siteMono[rows, k], pred, rr, mask, worst, nExcl, bestA, Nrow},\n  pred = Table[Product[sm[[A, s, siteIdx[[m, s]]]], {s, nL}], {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\n  pred = Table[pred[[m, A]]/pred[[vacIdx, A]], {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\n  rr = ratioM/pred;\n  bestA = Table[Ordering[Abs[pred[[m]]], -1][[1]], {m, nS}];\n  Nrow = Table[rr[[m, bestA[[m]]]], {m, nS}];\n  worst = Table[Max[Abs[rr[[m]]/Nrow[[m]] - 1]], {m, nS}];\n  {Max[worst], Min[Abs[pred]], Nrow}];\n{tims[\"wavefunction tests (3 conventions)\"], wfRes} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[wfTest @@ rk, {rk, {{{1, 2}, 1}, {{2, 3}, 3}, {{1, 3}, 2}}}]];\nchecks[\"wavefunction rule M_x (rows {1,2},k=1; {2,3},3; {1,3},2): max rel dev over 225 labels x 225 states\"] = wfRes[[All, 1]];\nNm = wfRes[[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"N_m the same for all three conventions (max rel diff)\"] = Max[Abs[wfRes[[1, 3]]/wfRes[[2, 3]] - 1], Abs[wfRes[[3, 3]]/wfRes[[2, 3]] - 1]];\nGrid[{{\"max rel dev of <x_m|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> vs N_m prod M (rows12 k1, rows23 k3, rows13 k2)\", N[wfRes[[All, 1]], 3]}, {\"min |predicted ratio| (zero-division guard)\", N[wfRes[[All, 2]], 3]}, {\"N_m identical across conventions (max rel diff)\", N[checks[\"N_m the same for all three conventions (max rel diff)\"], 3]}, {\"N_m: min, max abs\", N[{Min[Abs[Nm]], Max[Abs[Nm]]}, 4]}, {\"time (s): overlaps, tests\", {tims[\"SoV overlaps with kets\"], tims[\"wavefunction tests (3 conventions)\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 1 results\n\n| check | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] | [3,2,0] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B eigensystem (dense, prec 60): time (s); min gap of eigenvalues at u = 3/11 (simple spectrum) | 0.025; 1.6e-5 | 0.39; 4.8e-6 | 0.36; 6.5e-6 |\n| all six roots on the two ladders, 3 + 3 | True | True | True |\n| size of the rule set = dim V; every site triple of every state is in the rule set (both sites) | 8; True | 15; True | 15; True |\n| # distinct (site-1, site-2) label pairs (225 = bijection) | 64 | 225 | 225 |\n| vacuum pair ((lambda1|lambda1 lambda2), same) present; its index; x0 = e1 tensor e1 is an exact left eigenvector of B and parallel to that SoV covector | True; 1; True, 1e-60 | True; 1; True, 1e-60 | True; 1; True, 1e-60 |\n| wavefunction rule, max rel dev over all labels x all states: rows{1,2} k=1 / rows{2,3} k=3 / rows{1,3} k=2 | < 1e-43 / 1e-46 / 1e-46 | < 1e-39 / 1e-43 / 1e-43 | < 1e-40 / 1e-44 / 1e-44 |\n| min abs predicted ratio (zero-division guard); N_m identical across the three conventions (max rel diff) | 4.5e-3; < 1e-47 | 1.1e-5; < 1e-43 | 6.6e-7; < 1e-44 |\n| abs N_m range (min, max) | 0.054, 2.09 | 0.014, 4.77 | 0.0036, 8.23 |\n| timings (s): B(7 pts); roots (225 states); overlaps; wavefunction tests (3 conventions) | 0.04; 0.22; 0.02; 0.14 | 0.19; 1.6; 0.38; 1.5 | 0.18; 1.6; 0.36; 1.5 |\n\n**Verified label rule (all three reps, no exception):** SoV labels (a|bc), lambda2 <= a <= lambda1, 0 <= c <= lambda2, c <= b <= a (count 8, 15, 15 = dim V), root triple theta_s + {-1-a, -b, -c} h, sorted triple = (m1, m21, m22) = (-1-a, -b, -c); vacuum (lambda1|lambda1 lambda2) = triples (-3,-2,-1), (-4,-3,-1), (-4,-3,-2) for [2,1,0], [3,1,0], [3,2,0] (the known vacuum triples (4,3,1) and (4,3,2) of the spec). No shifted points are needed.\n\n**Verified wavefunction monomial (all three reps, all three conventions, no shift):** psi_x(B) = N_x prod_s M^(s)_x/M^(s)_vac with M_(a|bc) = minor(n, n') v_k(theta - ch), (n, n') = (-1-a, -b), minor(n, n') := det2[v(n'), v(n)]_(r1, r2) = v_r1(n') v_r2(n) - v_r2(n') v_r1(n) (my sign: no extra sign in N_x; the spec's det2[v(n), v(n')] differs by an overall -1), rows (r1, r2), k in the three conventions above; N_x state independent. Every Q-vector in the monomials sits at theta_s + m h with m in -1-lambda1..0 (lambda1 + 2 points).\n\nBijection label <-> sorted triple (same on both sites; printed by cell 9): [2,1,0]: (1|00) -> (-2,0,0), (1|10) -> (-2,-1,0), (1|11) -> (-2,-1,-1), (2|00) -> (-3,0,0), (2|10) -> (-3,-1,0), (2|20) -> (-3,-2,0), (2|11) -> (-3,-1,-1), (2|21) -> (-3,-2,-1). [3,1,0]: those eight plus (3|00) -> (-4,0,0), (3|10) -> (-4,-1,0), (3|20) -> (-4,-2,0), (3|30) -> (-4,-3,0), (3|11) -> (-4,-1,-1), (3|21) -> (-4,-2,-1), (3|31) -> (-4,-3,-1). [3,2,0]: (2|00), (2|10), (2|20), (2|11), (2|21) as above, (2|22) -> (-3,-2,-2), and the nine (3|bc) with c <= 2: (3|00), (3|10), (3|20), (3|30), (3|11), (3|21), (3|31), (3|22) -> (-4,-2,-2), (3|32) -> (-4,-3,-2).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Site-1 covectors tensor e1 in the L=2 SoV basis (Task 2)\n\nThe covectors e_nu tensor e1 (GT basis, nu = 1..dim V; a rotation covector e1 rho(g) is a polynomial combination of them) are expanded in the SoV basis (LinearSolve against the transposed left eigenvectors), multiplied by N_m (normalised-wavefunction units) and sorted by the site-2 label; `Kg[c2]` is the (dim V x dim V) rational matrix (rows nu, columns site-1 label x) of the SoV states with site-2 label (lambda1|lambda1 c2). Identity tested on all states: <cov tensor e1|Psi>/<x0|Psi> * M^(1)_vac = sum_c2 lambda2^(c2) sum_x (cov.Kg[c2])_x M^(1)_x (rows {2,3}, k = 3).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2: site-1 covectors tensor e1 in the L=2 SoV basis. K^(c2)[nu, x] = coefficient (in normalised-wavefunction units c_m N_m) of e_nu tensor e1 on the SoV state with site-1 label x and site-2 label (lambda1|lambda1 c2) *)\n{tims[\"expansion of e_nu tensor e1\"], cS} = AbsoluteTiming[LinearSolve[Transpose[vecB], Transpose[Table[N[UnitVector[d2, (nu - 1) d1 + 1], prec], {nu, d1}]]]];\nchecks[\"expansion error of e_nu tensor e1 in the SoV basis (max)\"] = Max[Abs[Transpose[vecB] . cS - Transpose[Table[UnitVector[d2, (nu - 1) d1 + 1], {nu, d1}]]]];\nKfull = cS * Nm;  (* d2 x d1, rows = SoV state m *)\nscaleK = Max[Abs[Kfull]];\nsuppM = Select[Range[nS], Max[Abs[Kfull[[#]]]]/scaleK > 10^-30 &];\nsite2Labs = Union[allLabs[[suppM, 2]]];\ngrp[c2_] := {-1 - Λ[[1]], -Λ[[1]], -c2};\ngrpSet = Table[grp[c2], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"site-2 labels in the support = {(lambda1|lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2}?\"] = {Length[site2Labs], Sort[site2Labs] === Sort[grpSet], Complement[site2Labs, grpSet]};\n(* label pair -> state index; the K matrices per site-2 group (rationalised, with the rationalisation error) *)\nmOfPair = Association[Table[allLabs[[m]] -> m, {m, nS}]];\nratz[x_] := Rationalize[Chop[x, 10^-40], 10^-40];\nKg = Association[Table[c2 -> Table[ratz[Kfull[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x]], grp[c2]}], nu]]], {nu, d1}, {x, d1}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nratErr = Max[Table[Max[Abs[N[Kg[c2], prec] - Table[Kfull[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x]], grp[c2]}], nu]], {nu, d1}, {x, d1}]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nchecks[\"K rationalisation error (max abs, prec 60 data)\"] = ratErr;\nchecks[\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\"] = Table[MatrixRank[Kg[c2]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"max denominator digits in K\"] = Max[Table[Max[IntegerLength /@ Flatten[Denominator[Kg[c2]]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\n(* lambda_2^(c2) = v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h), k-independence: v(theta2 - c2 h) parallel to v(theta2 - lambda2 h) *)\nfacL[A_, c2_] := vm[A, 2, -c2][[3]]/vm[A, 2, -Λ[[2]]][[3]];\nchecks[\"v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) independent of k (max rel spread over states, c2)\"] = Max[Table[Max[Abs[vm[A, 2, -c2]/vm[A, 2, -Λ[[2]]]/facL[A, c2] - 1]], {A, nS}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nchecks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) on both sites (2x2 minors, max)\"] = Max[Table[Norm[Flatten[Minors[Transpose[{vm[A, s, 0], vm[A, s, -1]}], 2]]]/(Norm[vm[A, s, 0]] Norm[vm[A, s, -1]]), {A, nS}, {s, nL}]];\n(* the overlap identity for covectors cov tensor e1:  <cov tensor e1|Psi>/<x0|Psi> * M1_vac = sum_c2 lambda2^(c2) sum_x (cov.K^(c2))_x M1_x, rows {2,3}, k = 3 *)\nsm23 = siteMono[{2, 3}, 3];\nvacL = labIdx[vacTrip];\novlExact[cov_, A_] := (kron[cov, e1] . ketC[[A]])/(x0C . ketC[[A]]);\novlK[cov_, A_] := Sum[facL[A, c2] Sum[(cov . Kg[c2])[[x]] sm23[[A, 1, x]], {x, d1}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nidDevK[cov_] := Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]] - ovlK[cov, A]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]]], {A, nS}]];\ngaussCov[{al_, be_, ga_}] := e1 . nexp[al Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[be Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[ga Ee[2, 3]];\nSeedRandom[11]; covRnd = RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, d1];\nchecks[\"overlap identity via K: max rel dev (generic Gauss rotation, random covector, 3 GT basis covectors)\"] = {idDevK[Normal[gaussCov[{2/3, -3/7, 5/4}]]], idDevK[covRnd], Max[Table[idDevK[uv[nu]], {nu, {1, 2, d1}}]]};\nGrid[{{\"expansion error\", N[checks[\"expansion error of e_nu tensor e1 in the SoV basis (max)\"], 3]}, {\"# SoV states in the support; site-2 labels (count, = groups?, extra)\", checks[\"site-2 labels in the support = {(lambda1|lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2}?\"]}, {\"K rationalisation error; max denominator digits\", {N[ratErr, 3], checks[\"max denominator digits in K\"]}}, {\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\", checks[\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\"]}, {\"k-independence of lambda2^(c2); v(th) || v(th-h)\", N[{checks[\"v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) independent of k (max rel spread over states, c2)\"], checks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) on both sites (2x2 minors, max)\"]}, 3]}, {\"overlap identity (rotation, random, basis)\", N[checks[\"overlap identity via K: max rel dev (generic Gauss rotation, random covector, 3 GT basis covectors)\"], 3]}, {\"# support states total, times (s)\", {Length[suppM], tims[\"expansion of e_nu tensor e1\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2 results\n\n| check | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] | [3,2,0] |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| expansion error of e_nu tensor e1 in the SoV basis (max abs) | 5e-90 | 6e-88 | 1.5e-86 |\n| site-2 labels in the support; equal to {(lambda1 \\| lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2}?; extra labels | 2; True; none | 2; True; none | 3; True; none |\n| # SoV states in the support (= sum of the ranks below) | 12 | 24 | 28 |\n| ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0, 1, .. (the last one = vacuum group c2 = lambda2) | 4, 8 | 9, 15 | 4, 9, 15 |\n| rationalisation error of K (max abs); max denominator digits | 1.4e-90; 4 | 5.1e-88; 5 | 4.6e-86; 6 |\n| lambda2^(c2) = v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) independent of k (max rel spread, all states, all c2) | < 1e-46 | < 1e-45 | < 1e-46 |\n| v(theta_s) parallel to v(theta_s - h) (2x2 minors, max, both sites, all states) | 5.5e-58 | 1.1e-57 | 2.0e-57 |\n| overlap identity via K, max rel dev over all states: generic Gauss rotation (2/3, -3/7, 5/4) / random integer covector / three GT basis covectors | < 1e-45 / 1e-48 / 1e-48 | < 1e-42 / 1e-47 / 1e-48 | < 1e-42 / 1e-46 / 1e-47 |\n| time (s) | 0.005 | 0.06 | 0.09 |\n\nResult: for every rep the site-2 labels that occur are exactly the vacuum (lambda1 \\| lambda1 lambda2) and (lambda1 \\| lambda1 c2), c2 < lambda2, with factors lambda2^(c2) (k-independent: the vectors v(theta2 - c h), c = 0..lambda2, are all parallel). The K matrices (exact rationals, entries with at most 4, 5, 6 digit denominators) are stored in `Kg`; they depend on (h, theta) only (Task 7).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Tensors and automatic bracket count (Task 3)\n\nMinors (n, n') (n < n') on the p = lambda1 + 2 points m = -1-lambda1..0 in colex order (12),(13),(23),(14),(24),(34),..., columns c = 0..lambda2. Tensor C^(c2)_{(nn'),c} = (cov.Kg[c2]) at the slot of the label (-1-a, -b, -c). A column is an antisymmetric p x p 2-form; rank 2r means r bracket determinants Bk2[F,G] = <Q^3 F><Q^2 G> - <Q^2 F><Q^3 G> are needed (for any covector: Schur-complement decomposition into r wedges), the automatic count is the sum of rank/2 over all columns of all groups. Tools tested: bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} minor_23(n,n') symbolically on all points; all 4x4 Pfaffians of F^G vanish and not of F1^G1 + F2^G2; 6x6 Pfaffian (synthetic 6-point forms) 0 for rank 4, nonzero for rank 6; `decompForm` reconstructs.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3: coefficient tensors C^(c2)_{(n n'), c} (rows = minors (n,n'), n<n', in colex order over the points m = -1-lambda1..0; columns c = 0..lambda2) and the automatic bracket count *)\nmnL = Flatten[Table[{mPts[[i]], mPts[[j]]}, {j, 2, pPts}, {i, 1, j - 1}], 1];\nnMin = Length[mnL];\nmnIdx[{n_, np_}] := First[Flatten[Position[mnL, {n, np}]]];\n(* tensorOf: phi = vector over site-1 labels (labRule order) -> nMin x (lambda2+1) matrix; label x = {n, n', -c} sits at slot ((n,n'), c) *)\ntensorOf[φ_] := Module[{CC = ConstantArray[0, {nMin, Λ[[2]] + 1}]}, Do[With[{l = labRule[[x]]}, CC[[mnIdx[{l[[1]], l[[2]]}], -l[[3]] + 1]] = φ[[x]]], {x, d1}]; CC];\n(* 2-form of a column vector as an antisymmetric pPts x pPts matrix, wedge of two vectors, Pfaffians, Schur-type decomposition into wedges *)\namat[A_] := Table[Which[i == j, 0, i < j, A[[mnIdx[{mPts[[i]], mPts[[j]]}]]], True, -A[[mnIdx[{mPts[[j]], mPts[[i]]}]]]], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}];\nwedgeV[F_, G_] := Table[F[[mi]] G[[mj]] - F[[mj]] G[[mi]], {mj, 2, pPts}, {mi, 1, mj - 1}] // Flatten;\npfaff[M_] := Module[{n = Length[M]}, If[n == 0, 1, If[OddQ[n], 0, Expand[Sum[(-1)^j M[[1, j]] pfaff[With[{r = Complement[Range[n], {1, j}]}, M[[r, r]]]], {j, 2, n}]]]]];\npf4list[A_] := With[{M = amat[A]}, Table[pfaff[M[[s, s]]], {s, Subsets[Range[pPts], {4}]}]];\npf6list[A_] := With[{M = amat[A]}, Table[pfaff[M[[s, s]]], {s, Subsets[Range[pPts], {6}]}]];\ndecompForm[A_] := Module[{M = amat[A], res = {}, ij, F, G, fw},\n  While[Not[AllTrue[Flatten[M], # === 0 &]],\n   ij = First[Select[Tuples[Range[pPts], 2], #[[1]] < #[[2]] && M[[#[[1]], #[[2]]]] =!= 0 &]];\n   F = M[[All, ij[[1]]]]/M[[ij[[1]], ij[[2]]]]; G = M[[All, ij[[2]]]];\n   AppendTo[res, {F, G}];\n   M = M - Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}]];\n  res];\n(* tool checks: bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} minor(n,n') on the whole point set (symbolic), Pfaffian criteria *)\nqS[j_, m_] := qq[j, m];\nminSym[{n_, np_}] := qS[2, np] qS[3, n] - qS[3, np] qS[2, n];\nbrQ[j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] qS[j, mPts[[i]]], {i, pPts}];\nBk2[F_, G_] := brQ[3, F] brQ[2, G] - brQ[2, F] brQ[3, G];\nFs0 = Array[ff, pPts]; Gs0 = Array[gg, pPts];\nchecks[\"bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum (F^G)_{nn'} minor_{23}(n,n'), symbolic on all points\"] = Expand[Bk2[Fs0, Gs0] - Sum[wedgeV[Fs0, Gs0][[i]] minSym[mnL[[i]]], {i, nMin}]] === 0;\nSeedRandom[5];\nrF = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rF2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rF3 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG3 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts];\nchecks[\"Pfaffian tools: F^G has all 4x4 Pfaffians 0; F1^G1 + F2^G2 does not; its Pfaffian rank is 4 (rank of amat)\"] = {Union[pf4list[wedgeV[rF, rG]]] === {0}, Union[pf4list[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]] =!= {0}, MatrixRank[amat[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]]};\n(* 6x6 Pfaffians on a synthetic 6-point form: rank <= 4 form has Pf6 = 0, rank-6 form does not (tool test independent of the rep) *)\nw6[F_, G_] := Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, 6}, {j, 6}];\na4 = w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]] + w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]]; a6 = a4 + w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]];\nchecks[\"6x6 Pfaffian: rank-4 form 0, rank-6 form nonzero\"] = {pfaff[a4], pfaff[a6] =!= 0};\nchecks[\"decompForm reconstructs random rank-4 form\"] = (Total[wedgeV[#[[1]], #[[2]]] & /@ decompForm[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]] === wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]);\n(* tensors at a generic rational rotation and at a random covector; rank of every column's 2-form *)\ngen0 = {2/3, -3/7, 5/4};\ncovGen = Normal[gaussCov[gen0]];\ntensorsOf[cov_] := Association[Table[c2 -> tensorOf[cov . Kg[c2]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\ntenGen = tensorsOf[covGen]; tenRnd = tensorsOf[covRnd];\ncolRank[T_, c_] := MatrixRank[amat[T[[All, c + 1]]]];\nrankTab[ten_] := Table[Table[colRank[ten[c2], c], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nrkGen = rankTab[tenGen]; rkRnd = rankTab[tenRnd];\nsupportTab = Table[Table[Union[Flatten[mnL[[Flatten[Position[tenGen[c2][[All, c + 1]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]]], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nslotsTab = Table[Table[Count[tenGen[c2][[All, c + 1]], x_ /; x =!= 0], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"rank of each column 2-form, generic rotation, per group c2 (rows) and column c\"] = rkGen;\nchecks[\"rank of each column 2-form, random covector\"] = rkRnd;\nautoGen = Total[Flatten[rkGen]]/2; autoRnd = Total[Flatten[rkRnd]]/2;\nchecks[\"automatic bracket count (generic rotation, random covector)\"] = {autoGen, autoRnd};\nchecks[\"tensor identity: sum over groups lambda2^(c2) sum_{nn',c} C minor v_k(-c) = overlap * M1vac (generic rotation, 225 states, rows 23, k 3)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[covGen, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]] - Sum[facL[A, c2] Sum[tenGen[c2][[mi, c + 1]] (vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 2]]][[2]] vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 1]]][[3]] - vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 2]]][[3]] vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 1]]][[2]]) vm[A, 1, -c][[3]], {mi, nMin}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[covGen, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]]], {A, nS}]];\nGrid[{{\"points (m), # minors, columns\", {mPts, nMin, Λ[[2]] + 1}}, {\"tool checks (bracket identity; Pfaffians; 6x6; decompForm)\", {checks[\"bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum (F^G)_{nn'} minor_{23}(n,n'), symbolic on all points\"], checks[\"Pfaffian tools: F^G has all 4x4 Pfaffians 0; F1^G1 + F2^G2 does not; its Pfaffian rank is 4 (rank of amat)\"], checks[\"6x6 Pfaffian: rank-4 form 0, rank-6 form nonzero\"], checks[\"decompForm reconstructs random rank-4 form\"]}}, {\"support points per (group c2, column c) at the generic rotation\", supportTab}, {\"populated slots per (c2, c), generic rotation\", slotsTab}, {\"column ranks, generic rotation (rows c2 = 0..lambda2, columns c = 0..lambda2)\", rkGen}, {\"column ranks, random covector\", rkRnd}, {\"automatic bracket count per group c2 (generic rotation)\", Total[#]/2 & /@ rkGen}, {\"automatic bracket count: generic rotation, random covector; dim V, |Lambda|\", {autoGen, autoRnd, d1, Total[Λ]}}, {\"tensor identity (225 states) rel dev\", N[checks[\"tensor identity: sum over groups lambda2^(c2) sum_{nn',c} C minor v_k(-c) = overlap * M1vac (generic rotation, 225 states, rows 23, k 3)\"], 3]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 3 results\n\nTool checks (all reps): bracket identity True, Pfaffian tools True (rank of F1^G1 + F2^G2 = 4), 6x6 Pfaffian {0, True}, decomposition reconstructs True. Tensor identity (all states, generic rotation (2/3, -3/7, 5/4), rows {2,3}, k = 3): < 1e-45 / 1e-42 / 1e-42. No column has 6 or more support points (so rank <= 4 is automatic where a column has 5 points).\n\n**[2,1,0]** (points -3..0, 6 minors): group c2 = 0: column 0 on {-3,-2,-1} (3 slots, rank 2), column 1 on {-3,-2} (1 slot, rank 2); group c2 = 1 (vacuum): column 0 on {-3,-2,-1,0} (5 slots, rank 4), column 1 on {-3,-2,-1} (3 slots, rank 2). Brackets per group: 2, 3; total **5** (generic rotation and random covector alike); dim V = 8, |Lambda| = 3.\n\n**[3,1,0]** (points -4..0, 10 minors): group 0: column 0 on {-4,..,-1} (6 slots, rank 4), column 1 on {-4,-3,-2} (3 slots, rank 2); group 1 (vacuum): column 0 on {-4,..,0} (9 slots, rank 4), column 1 on {-4,..,-1} (6 slots, rank 4). Brackets per group: 3, 4; total **7** (generic rotation = random covector); dim V = 15, |Lambda| = 4.\n\n**[3,2,0]** (points -4..0, 10 minors, 3 columns): group 0: columns 0, 1, 2 on {-4,-3,-2} (3 slots, rank 2), {-4,-3} (1 slot, rank 2), empty (rank 0); group 1: {-4,..,-1} (5 slots, rank 4), {-4,-3,-2} (3 slots, rank 2), {-4,-3} (1 slot, rank 2); group 2 (vacuum): {-4,..,0} (7 slots, rank 4), {-4,..,-1} (5 slots, rank 4), {-4,-3,-2} (3 slots, rank 2). Brackets per group: 2, 4, 5; total **11** (generic = random); dim V = 15, |Lambda| = 5.\n\nSo the automatic count is 5, 7, 11 for |Lambda| = 3, 4, 5 and dim V = 8, 15, 15: set by the ladder length and the ranks, not by dim V (it is below dim V in every case: 5/8, 7/15, 11/15). The rank pattern is the same for a generic rotation and for a random covector (not a rotation).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Loci in the Gauss chart (Task 4)\n\nSymbolic tensors: gaussCov(gA, gB, gC) = e1 rho(exp(gA E12) exp(gB E13) exp(gC E23)) is a polynomial row vector (orbit check: Jacobian rank 3 at the generic point for all three reps, i.e. the orbit of e1 is 3-dimensional); C^(c2) = tensorOf(gaussCov . Kg[c2]) is polynomial. Per column the 4x4 Pfaffians (decomposable <=> all vanish) are factored; the ideal is saturated by gA gB gC (Groebner, 120 s limit per solve, none timed out) to get the genuine part; dim V(I) = largest set of variables with trivial elimination ideal. Joint loci per group and over all groups cell 20; cell 21 = natural-guess test: factors of the conic form gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 (b1 b3 = cc b2^2 on b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC)) against cc(t - k), cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4a: symbolic tensors in the Gauss chart g = exp(gA E12) exp(gB E13) exp(gC E23) (first row of the 3x3 unipotent: b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC)); polynomial in (gA, gB, gC) *)\ngVars = {gA, gB, gC};\n{tims[\"symbolic covector and tensors\"], gaussCovS} = AbsoluteTiming[Expand /@ Normal[e1 . nexp[gA Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[gB Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[gC Ee[2, 3]]]];\nchecks[\"symbolic Gauss covector at gen0 equals the numeric one\"] = (gaussCovS /. Thread[gVars -> gen0]) === covGen;\nchecks[\"orbit of e1 in the Gauss chart: Jacobian rank at gen0 (3 = 3-dimensional orbit)\"] = MatrixRank[Table[D[gaussCovS, v] /. Thread[gVars -> gen0], {v, gVars}]];\ntenS = Association[Table[c2 -> tensorOf[Expand /@ (gaussCovS . Kg[c2])], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\ncolS[c2_, c_] := tenS[c2][[All, c + 1]];\nsupPts[c2_, c_] := Union[Flatten[mnL[[Flatten[Position[colS[c2, c], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]]];\n(* dimension of the zero set of an ideal (over C) in the Gauss chart: largest subset S of variables with trivial elimination ideal; a vanishing ideal ({} or {0}) has dimension 3 *)\ndimOf[gens_List] := Module[{gb, vars = gVars, best = -1}, Do[If[Length[S] > best, With[{el = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[gens, S, Complement[vars, S]], 120, $Failed]}, If[el === $Failed, best = \"timeout\", If[(el === {} || el === {0}) && NumberQ[best], best = Length[S]]]]], {S, Reverse[Subsets[vars]]}]; best];\n(* genuine part (alpha beta gamma != 0): saturate by gA gB gC *)\nsatGen[gens_List] := TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[Append[gens, 1 - wSat gA gB gC], gVars, {wSat}], 120, $Failed];\ncolPf[c2_, c_] := DeleteCases[Union[Factor /@ pf4list[colS[c2, c]]], 0];\n{tims[\"column Pfaffians\"], pfTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[{c2, c, Length[supPts[c2, c]], colPf[c2, c]}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"orbit of e1: Jacobian rank at gen0\", checks[\"orbit of e1 in the Gauss chart: Jacobian rank at gen0 (3 = 3-dimensional orbit)\"], \"\", \"\"}, {\"group c2\", \"column c\", \"# support points\", \"4x4 Pfaffians (factored, nonzero, distinct)\"}}, Flatten[pfTab, 1]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4b: exact loci in the Gauss chart. Per column: ideal of 4x4 Pfaffians (\"column decomposable\"), dimension of its zero set, genuine part (gA gB gC != 0, by saturation) and its dimension; then the joint loci per group and over all groups. Gröbner solves are time-limited (120 s each). *)\ndimOf[gens_List] := Module[{gb, best = 0, el, ok = True},\n  If[gens === {}, Return[3]];\n  gb = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[gens, gVars], 120, $Failed];\n  If[gb === $Failed, Return[\"timeout\"]]; If[gb === {1}, Return[-1]];\n  Do[If[Length[S] > best, el = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[gens, S, Complement[gVars, S]], 120, $Failed];\n     If[el === $Failed, ok = False, If[el === {} || el === {0}, best = Length[S]]]], {S, Reverse[Rest[Subsets[gVars]]]}];\n  If[ok, best, {\"at least\", best}]];\nsatGen[gens_List] := If[gens === {}, {}, TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[Append[gens, 1 - wSat gA gB gC], gVars, {wSat}], 120, $Failed]];\ndimGen[sat_] := If[sat === $Failed, \"timeout\", dimOf[sat]];\nlociRow[name_, gens_List] := Module[{sat = satGen[gens]}, {name, If[gens === {}, \"automatic\", gens], dimOf[gens], If[sat === $Failed, \"timeout\", If[sat === {1}, \"empty\", Factor /@ sat]], dimGen[sat]}];\n{tims[\"column loci\"], lociCol} = AbsoluteTiming[Flatten[Table[lociRow[\"group \" <> ToString[c2] <> \", column \" <> ToString[c], colPf[c2, c]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1]];\ngrpGens[c2_] := DeleteCases[Union[Flatten[Table[colPf[c2, c], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1]], 0];\nallGens = DeleteCases[Union[Flatten[Table[grpGens[c2], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1]], 0];\n{tims[\"joint loci\"], lociJoint} = AbsoluteTiming[Join[Table[lociRow[\"joint: all columns of group \" <> ToString[c2] <> If[c2 == Λ[[2]], \" (vacuum, R2delta analogue)\", \"\"], grpGens[c2]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {lociRow[\"joint: all columns of all groups\", allGens]}]];\nchecks[\"columns with 6 or more support points (rank <= 4 loci needed)\"] = Select[Flatten[Table[{c2, c, Length[supPts[c2, c]]}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1], #[[3]] >= 6 &];\nGrid[Join[{{\"columns with >= 6 support points (rank <= 4 locus needed; none means rank <= 4 is automatic)\", checks[\"columns with 6 or more support points (rank <= 4 loci needed)\"], \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"locus\", \"generators (4x4 Pfaffians)\", \"dim V(I)\", \"genuine part (saturated ideal)\", \"dim genuine\"}}, lociCol, lociJoint], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4d: the natural guess. The adjoint quadric is 2(t-2) b1 b3 = (t-3) b2^2 on the first row b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC) of g, i.e. gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 with cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)). Which irreducible factors of the column Pfaffians are of this conic form, with which cc, and does cc match cc(t - k) for a small shift k? *)\nallFactors = Select[DeleteDuplicates[Flatten[Table[{c2, c, #[[1]]} & /@ Flatten[FactorList[#][[2 ;;]] & /@ colPf[c2, c], 1], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2], #1[[1 ;; 2]] === #2[[1 ;; 2]] && (#1[[3]] === #2[[3]] || #1[[3]] === -#2[[3]]) &], Not[FreeQ[#[[3]], gA | gB | gC]] &];\nconicOf[f_] := Module[{p = Expand[f], k},\n  If[Exponent[p, gB] == 1 && Exponent[p, gC] == 1 && Exponent[p, gA] == 2 && FreeQ[Coefficient[p, gB, 1], gA | gB | gC], k = Coefficient[p, gB, 1]; With[{rem = Expand[p/k - (gB + gA gC)]}, If[FreeQ[rem, gB | gC] && Exponent[rem, gA] == 2 && Coefficient[rem, gA, 1] === 0 && Coefficient[rem, gA, 0] === 0, -Coefficient[rem, gA, 2], None]], None]];\nccGuess[tv_] := (tv - 3)/(2 (tv - 2));\nconicTab = Select[Table[{f[[1]], f[[2]], f[[3]], conicOf[f[[3]]]}, {f, allFactors}], #[[4]] =!= None &];\nnonConic = Select[Table[{f[[1]], f[[2]], f[[3]]}, {f, allFactors}], conicOf[#[[3]]] === None && Not[MatchQ[#[[3]], gA | gB | gC]] &];\nshiftMatch = Table[{c[[1 ;; 2]], c[[4]], Select[Range[-4, 4], ccGuess[tPar - #] === c[[4]] &], Select[Range[-4, 4], ccGuess[tPar + #] === c[[4]] &]}, {c, conicTab}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"conic-type factors  (gB + gA gC) = cc gA^2:  {group, column, factor, cc}\", \"\"}}, {#[[1 ;; 2]], {#[[3]], #[[4]]}} & /@ conicTab, {{\"t = theta12/h, adjoint guess cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) at this t\", {tPar, ccGuess[tPar]}}, {\"matches of cc with cc(t - k) / cc(t + k), k in -4..4: {col, cc, k's, k's}\", shiftMatch}, {\"other (non-conic, non-monomial) irreducible factors {group, column, factor}\", nonConic}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 4 results (Gauss chart; Pf = 4x4 Pfaffians of the column 2-form; \"dim\" = dimension of the zero set in C^3 including degenerate parts; \"genuine\" = part with gA gB gC != 0)\n\nAll Gröbner solves took well under 1 s (no timeout, no fallback). Orbit of e1: Jacobian rank 3 (all reps). No column has >= 6 support points.\n\n**[2,1,0] (regression).** Only column (c2 = 1, c = 0) (4 points) is not automatic: Pf = (4/837) gB^2 (43 gA^2 - 16 gB - 16 gA gC) -> locus {gB = 0} u {16 (gB + gA gC) = 43 gA^2}, dim 2; genuine part: the quadric 16 (gB + gA gC) = 43 gA^2 only (dim 2). 43/16 = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) at t = 62/35: **reproduced**. Joint loci: group 0 automatic (dim 3); vacuum group and all groups: the quadric (dim 2). Factor test: cc = 43/16 = cc(t - 0).\n\n**[3,1,0].** Non-automatic columns: (0,0) [4 points], (1,0) [5 points, vacuum group], (1,1) [4 points, vacuum group].\n- (0,0): Pf = (52675/4464) gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2); genuine: two components {gA^2 = gB + gA gC} (cc = 1, i.e. b2^2 = b1 b3) and {3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2 = 0}, dim 2 each.\n- (1,1): Pf = -(43/18)(39 gA^2 - 4 gB - 4 gA gC)(gA^2 - gB - gA gC); genuine: {gB + gA gC = (39/4) gA^2} and {gA^2 = gB + gA gC}, dim 2 each.\n- (1,0) (5 points): five 4x4 Pfaffians, each a product of conic factors (cc = 52/43, 43/16, 1433/344, 1), gB + gA gC and two further polynomial factors (printed in cell 20/21 outputs); dim V = 1 (degenerate points only) and **the genuine part is EMPTY**: no genuine rotation makes the vacuum group's column c = 0 decomposable. Hence the (R2delta) analogue (all columns of the vacuum group decomposable) and the joint locus of all groups contain no genuine rotation. [The adjoint quadric 16 (gB + gA gC) = 43 gA^2 is one factor of one Pfaffian of this column.]\n- Joint: group 0 = column (0,0) locus (dim 2); vacuum group: empty; all groups: empty. Rank <= 4 is automatic for the 5-point column.\n\n**[3,2,0].** Non-automatic columns: (1,0) [4 points], (2,0) [5 points, vacuum group], (2,1) [4 points, vacuum group]; (0,*), (1,1), (1,2), (2,2) automatic; group 0 column 2 is identically zero.\n- (1,0): Pf = (210700/730701) gB^3 (117 gA^2 gB - 86 gB^2 - 43 gA gB gC + 43 gA^2 gC^2); genuine: the hypersurface 117 gA^2 gB - 86 gB^2 - 43 gA gB gC + 43 gA^2 gC^2 = 0 (non-conic), dim 2.\n- (2,1): Pf = -(14792/7533) gB^2 (39 gA^2 - 8 gB - 8 gA gC); genuine: {gB + gA gC = (39/8) gA^2} (conic), dim 2.\n- (2,0) (5 points): three independent 4x4 Pfaffians (factors in the cell 20/21 outputs); genuine part = the **curve** {1247689 gB = 461332 gC^2, 1117 gA = -194 gC} (dim 1).\n- Joint: vacuum group (all three columns): **empty** (the curve of (2,0) is not on the conic of (2,1)); all groups: empty. Pairs of columns: {(1,0),(2,1)}: the curve {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC} (dim 1); {(1,0),(2,0)} and {(2,0),(2,1)}: empty.\n\n**Natural guess (cell 21).** Conic-type factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 with their cc at t = 62/35: [2,1,0]: 43/16 (= cc(t), shift 0). [3,1,0]: column (0,0): 1; (1,0): 52/43, 43/16, 1433/344, 1; (1,1): 39/4, 1. [3,2,0]: (2,0): 13/2; (2,1): 39/8. Only the adjoint factor 43/16 occurring in [3,1,0] (1,0) equals cc(t - k) (k = 0); no other factor equals cc(t - k) or cc(t + k) for k in 1..4, so the adjoint quadric does not generalise by a simple shift t -> t - k. Non-conic factors: [3,1,0]: gB + gA gC (b3 = 0) and two high-degree factors in (1,0), the gB-quadratic factor of (0,0); [3,2,0]: the (1,0) factor above and two further factors in (2,0). The t-dependence of the conic constants (Moebius in t) is in Task 7.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Reduced forms: which column sets can be made decomposable by a genuine rotation, explicit bracket forms, 225-state verification (Tasks 4 and 5)\n\nCell 24: scan of all subsets S of the non-automatic columns (smallest first, supersets of an empty genuine locus pruned), genuine components (common factor / remaining ideal), rational points (grid search, FindInstance fallback) and bracket counts at the points (exact rank of every column 2-form). Cell 25: for a generic rotation and for every genuine locus component (first point) and for the best locus (all its points): exact Schur decomposition of every column into wedges F^G, then the full overlap  <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> * M^(1)_vac = sum_c2 lambda2^(c2) sum_c sum_(F,G) Bk2[F,G] Q^3(theta1 - c h)  evaluated numerically (prec 60) and compared with the exact overlap on all states (rows {2,3}, k = 3; max |lhs - rhs|/max |lhs|).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4c/5a: which sets of columns can be made decomposable simultaneously by a genuine rotation? Scan the subsets S of the non-automatic columns (smallest first; supersets of an empty genuine locus are skipped), keep the non-empty genuine loci, split them into irreducible-looking components (common factor / remaining ideal), find rational points and count brackets there. *)\nnontriv = Select[Flatten[Table[{c2, c}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1], colPf[#[[1]], #[[2]]] =!= {} &];\nsubsetGens[S_] := DeleteCases[Union[Flatten[colPf @@@ S, 1]], 0];\nscanT0 = AbsoluteTime[]; emptiesL = {}; nonEmptyL = {}; unresolvedL = {};\nDo[Do[\n   If[AbsoluteTime[] - scanT0 < 900 && Not[AnyTrue[emptiesL, SubsetQ[S, #] &]],\n    With[{sat = satGen[subsetGens[S]]},\n     Which[sat === $Failed, AppendTo[unresolvedL, S], sat === {1}, AppendTo[emptiesL, S], True, AppendTo[nonEmptyL, {S, sat}]]]], {S, Subsets[nontriv, {size}]}], {size, 1, Length[nontriv]}];\ntims[\"subset scan\"] = AbsoluteTime[] - scanT0;\nmaximalNE = Select[nonEmptyL, Function[e, Not[AnyTrue[nonEmptyL, #[[1]] =!= e[[1]] && SubsetQ[#[[1]], e[[1]]] &]]]];\n(* rational points with gA gB gC nonzero on {sat = 0}: a grid search solving for one variable (simplest points first), FindInstance as fallback *)\nratGrid = {1, 2, -1, 3, 1/2, -2, 3/2, 4, -3, 2/3, 5, -1/2};\nratPoints[sat_List, nWant_: 2] := Module[{pts = {}, fi, sol, pt},\n  Do[If[Length[pts] < nWant,\n    Do[sol = Quiet[Solve[And @@ ((# == 0) & /@ (sat /. {fs[[1]] -> a1v, fs[[2]] -> a2v})), fs[[3]]]];\n     If[ListQ[sol], Do[pt = gVars /. Join[{fs[[1]] -> a1v, fs[[2]] -> a2v}, s]; If[VectorQ[pt, Element[#, Rationals] && # =!= 0 &], pts = Union[pts, {pt}]], {s, sol}]], {a1v, ratGrid}, {a2v, ratGrid}]], {fs, {{gA, gC, gB}, {gA, gB, gC}, {gB, gC, gA}}}];\n  If[pts === {}, fi = TimeConstrained[FindInstance[And @@ ((# == 0) & /@ sat) && gA gB gC != 0, gVars, Rationals, nWant], 40, {}]; If[ListQ[fi] && fi =!= {}, pts = Union[gVars /. fi]]];\n  Take[SortBy[pts, LeafCount], UpTo[nWant]]];\nrankMat[pt_] := Table[MatrixRank[amat[tensorOf[Normal[gaussCov[pt]] . Kg[c2]][[All, c + 1]]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\n(* components: a common polynomial factor of the generators gives hypersurface components; the remaining ideal (generators divided by the gcd) the rest *)\nsplitLocus[sat_List] := Module[{g = If[Length[sat] == 1, sat[[1]], PolynomialGCD @@ sat], facs, rest, out},\n  facs = Select[FactorList[g][[All, 1]], Not[FreeQ[#, gA | gB | gC]] &];\n  rest = If[Length[sat] == 1, {}, Select[Together /@ (sat/g), # =!= 0 &]];\n  out = ({#} &) /@ facs;\n  If[rest =!= {} && GroebnerBasis[rest, gVars] =!= {1} && (Length[facs] == 0 || Length[sat] > 1), AppendTo[out, rest]];\n  If[out === {}, {sat}, out]];\nallComps = DeleteDuplicatesBy[Flatten[splitLocus /@ (nonEmptyL[[All, 2]]), 1], Expand[#] & /@ # &];\n{tims[\"components: points and counts\"], compTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{pts = ratPoints[comp, 4]}, {comp, dimOf[comp], pts, rankMat /@ pts, (Total[Flatten[rankMat[#]]]/2) & /@ pts}], {comp, allComps}]];\n{tims[\"maximal column sets: points\"], maxTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{S = e[[1]], sat = e[[2]]}, With[{pts = ratPoints[sat, 2]}, {S, dimOf[sat], Factor /@ sat, pts, (Total[Flatten[rankMat[#]]]/2) & /@ pts}]], {e, maximalNE}]];\nchecks[\"generic rotation: ranks, automatic bracket count\"] = {rankMat[gen0], Total[Flatten[rankMat[gen0]]]/2};\nGrid[Join[{{\"component of a genuine locus (ideal, Gauss chart)\", \"dim\", \"rational points (genuine)\", \"brackets at the points\"}}, {Factor /@ #[[1]], #[[2]], #[[3]], #[[5]]} & /@ compTab, {{\"maximal column sets S = {{group,column}} decomposable together, genuine ideal, dim, points -> counts\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, {#[[1]], #[[2]], Factor /@ #[[3]], {#[[4]], #[[5]]}} & /@ maxTab, {{\"minimal empty column sets (no genuine rotation)\", emptiesL, \"\", \"\"}, {\"unresolved (timeout)\", unresolvedL, \"\", \"\"}, {\"non-automatic columns\", nontriv, \"\", \"\"}, {\"generic rotation: ranks, count\", checks[\"generic rotation: ranks, automatic bracket count\"], \"\", \"\"}, {\"times (s): scan, components, maximal sets\", {tims[\"subset scan\"], tims[\"components: points and counts\"], tims[\"maximal column sets: points\"]}, \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 5: explicit bracket forms and the full overlap identity, all states. Per (group c2, column c) the 2-form is decomposed exactly into wedges F^G (Schur-complement elimination); the overlap is  sum_{c2} lambda2^(c2) sum_c sum_(F,G) Bk2[F,G] Q^3(theta1 - c h)  with Bk2[F,G] = <Q^3 F><Q^2 G> - <Q^2 F><Q^3 G>, <Q^j F> = sum_m F_m Q^j(theta1 + m h) *)\nbrN[A_, j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] vm[A, 1, mPts[[i]]][[j]], {i, pPts}];\nbk2N[A_, F_, G_] := brN[A, 3, F] brN[A, 2, G] - brN[A, 2, F] brN[A, 3, G];\nformData[pt_] := Module[{cov = Normal[gaussCov[pt]], ten, decs, rhs, lhs, recOK},\n  ten = tensorsOf[cov];\n  decs = Flatten[Table[Map[{c2, c, #[[1]], #[[2]]} &, decompForm[ten[c2][[All, c + 1]]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2];\n  recOK = AllTrue[Flatten[Table[Total[Join[{ConstantArray[0, nMin]}, wedgeV[#[[3]], #[[4]]] & /@ Select[decs, #[[1]] == c2 && #[[2]] == c &]]] === ten[c2][[All, c + 1]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}]], TrueQ];\n  lhs = Table[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]], {A, nS}];\n  rhs = Table[Sum[facL[A, d[[1]]] bk2N[A, d[[3]], d[[4]]] vm[A, 1, -d[[2]]][[3]], {d, decs}], {A, nS}];\n  {Length[decs], Max[Abs[lhs - rhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]], recOK, decs}];\n{tims[\"forms: generic rotation\"], fdGen} = AbsoluteTiming[formData[gen0]];\nbestRow = If[compTab === {}, {}, First[SortBy[compTab, {Min[#[[5]]], -#[[2]]} &]]];\nbestPts = If[bestRow === {}, {}, Pick[bestRow[[3]], bestRow[[5]], Min[bestRow[[5]]]]];\nbestName = If[bestRow === {}, \"none\", ToString[Factor /@ bestRow[[1]], InputForm] <> \" (dim \" <> ToString[bestRow[[2]]] <> \")\"];\n{tims[\"forms: best locus\"], fdBest} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[formData[pt], {pt, bestPts}]];\n{tims[\"forms: every locus component, first point\"], fdAll} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[formData[comp[[3, 1]]], {comp, compTab}]];\nchecks[\"generic rotation: # brackets, 225-state deviation, exact decomposition ok\"] = fdGen[[1 ;; 3]];\nchecks[\"best locus: # brackets, deviation, exact decomposition ok, per point\"] = fdBest[[All, 1 ;; 3]];\n(* the explicit measures at the first best point, per (group, column): F and G on the points m = -1-lambda1..0 *)\nfgList[fd_] := Map[{\"group \" <> ToString[#[[1]]], \"column \" <> ToString[#[[2]]], #[[3]], #[[4]]} &, fd[[4]]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"case\", \"# bracket determinants\", \"max rel dev over all 225 states\", \"exact decomposition\", \"dim V, |Lambda|\"}, {\"generic rotation \" <> ToString[gen0, InputForm], fdGen[[1]], N[fdGen[[2]], 3], fdGen[[3]], {d1, Total[Λ]}}}, Table[{\"best locus \" <> bestName <> \", point \" <> ToString[bestPts[[i]], InputForm], fdBest[[i, 1]], N[fdBest[[i, 2]], 3], fdBest[[i, 3]], \"\"}, {i, Length[bestPts]}], {{\"explicit measures at the first best point: {group, column, F, G} over points m = \" <> ToString[mPts], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, If[fdBest === {}, {}, Map[{#[[1]] <> \", \" <> #[[2]], #[[3]], #[[4]], \"\", \"\"} &, fgList[fdBest[[1]]]]], {{\"every locus component, first point: {component, point} -> # brackets, deviation\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, Table[{ToString[Factor /@ compTab[[i, 1]], InputForm] <> \" (dim \" <> ToString[compTab[[i, 2]]] <> \")\", ToString[compTab[[i, 3, 1]], InputForm], fdAll[[i, 1]], N[fdAll[[i, 2]], 3], fdAll[[i, 3]]}, {i, Length[compTab]}], {{\"times (s)\", tims[\"forms: generic rotation\"], tims[\"forms: best locus\"], \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Tasks 4c / 5 results\n\n**Genuine locus components, their dimension, a rational point and the bracket count there** (automatic generic count in the last column; counts are exact ranks / 2, deviation = max rel dev of the explicit F^G form against the exact overlap over ALL states):\n\n| rep | locus component (Gauss chart, genuine) | dim | rational point | # brackets (generic) | deviation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [2,1,0] | generic rotation (2/3, -3/7, 5/4) | 3 | | 5 (dim V = 8, \\|Lambda\\| = 3) | < 1e-45 |\n| [2,1,0] | 43 gA^2 = 16 (gB + gA gC) (column (1,0)) | 2 | (4, 23, 5), (4, 27, 4), (4, 31, 3), (4, 35, 2) | **4** | < 1e-48 (all four points) |\n| [3,1,0] | generic rotation (2/3, -3/7, 5/4) | 3 | | 7 (dim V = 15, \\|Lambda\\| = 4) | < 1e-42 |\n| [3,1,0] | gA^2 = gB + gA gC (columns (0,0) and (1,1) together; cc = 1) | 2 | (-3, 3, -2), (-3, 6, -1), (-3, 12, 1), (-3, 15, 2) | **5** | < 1e-46 |\n| [3,1,0] | 3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2 = 0 (column (0,0) only) | 2 | (-3, -3, 2) | 6 | < 1e-45 |\n| [3,1,0] | 39 gA^2 = 4 (gB + gA gC) (column (1,1) only) | 2 | (-2, 33, -3) | 6 | < 1e-47 |\n| [3,1,0] | curve {243 gB = 280 gC^2, 351 gA = 140 gC} ((0,0) and (1,1) together) | 1 | (-385, 2147145/2, -3861/4), (-127, 8177403/70, -44577/140) | **5** | < 1e-43 |\n| [3,2,0] | generic rotation (2/3, -3/7, 5/4) | 3 | | 11 (dim V = 15, \\|Lambda\\| = 5) | < 1e-42 |\n| [3,2,0] | 117 gA^2 gB - 86 gB^2 - 43 gA gB gC + 43 gA^2 gC^2 = 0 (column (1,0) only) | 2 | (-384, 8626176/43, -22464/43) | 10 | < 1e-42 |\n| [3,2,0] | 39 gA^2 = 8 (gB + gA gC) (column (2,1) only) | 2 | (4, 58, 5) | 10 | < 1e-46 |\n| [3,2,0] | curve {1247689 gB = 461332 gC^2, 1117 gA = -194 gC} (column (2,0) only) | 1 | (-385, 176239525/97, 430045/194) | 10 | < 1e-42 |\n| [3,2,0] | curve {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC} (columns (1,0) and (2,1) together) | 1 | (1, 559/280, 403/140), (-385, 2367365/8, -4433/4) | **9** | < 1e-46, < 1e-42 |\n\nMaximal column sets decomposable together by a genuine rotation: [2,1,0]: {(1,0)} (dim 2); [3,1,0]: {(0,0),(1,1)} (dim 2: the locus is {gA^2 = gB + gA gC} u the curve above); [3,2,0]: {(2,0)} and {(1,0),(2,1)} (both dim 1). Minimal sets with no genuine rotation: [2,1,0]: none; [3,1,0]: {(1,0)} (the vacuum group's 5-point column); [3,2,0]: {(1,0),(2,0)} and {(2,0),(2,1)}. Subset scan 0.02 s, components + points 0.03 / 0.42 / 1.1 s; no timeouts.\n\n**Best reduced forms** (fewest brackets): [2,1,0]: 4 = generic 5 - 1 on the quadric (2-dim family of genuine rotations; this reproduces the earlier adjoint result: four brackets and two Q^3 point values). [3,1,0]: **5 = generic 7 - 2** on the 2-dim family gA^2 = gB + gA gC (b2^2 = b1 b3: b = (1, gA, gA^2)), per group 2 + 3 (group 0: both columns rank 2; vacuum group: column 0 rank 4, column 1 rank 2); the same count 5 on the 1-dim curve. [3,2,0]: **9 = generic 11 - 2**, only on the 1-dim curve {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC} (a 1-parameter family of genuine rotations; every 2-dim locus gives only 10); the vacuum group (R2delta analogue) is never fully decomposable.\n\n**Explicit measures** (F, G over the points m = -1-lambda1..0, (group c2, column c); rows are the wedges F^G; the overlap is the sum of lambda2^(c2) Bk2[F,G] Q^3(theta1 - c h)):\n\n[2,1,0], point (4, 23, 5): (0,0): F = (0,-1,828/31,0), G = (-35/9,0,-276920/837,0); (0,1): F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (-6790/837,0,0,0); (1,0): F = (0,-1,248/909,-368/101), G = (-101/31,0,172/9,-7912/31); (1,1): F = (0,-1,-64/27,0), G = (1,0,344/9,0) (deviation < 1e-48, 4 brackets).\n\n[3,1,0], point (-3, 3, -2): (0,0): F = (0,0,0,-1,0), G = (-2835/62, -365715/248, 40635/62, 0, 0); (0,1): F = (0,-1,4/3,0,0), G = (-10185/248, 0, -145985/124, 0, 0); (1,0): [F = (0,-1,-9,0,-27), G = (43/62,0,-1161/31,-27,-10449/62)] + [F = (0,0,0,-1,0), G = (0,0,8505/8,0,-729)]; (1,1): F = (0,-1,-387/8,43,0), G = (1,0,-369,344,0) (deviation < 1e-47, 5 brackets).\n\n[3,2,0], point (1, 559/280, 403/140) (9 brackets, deviation < 1e-46): (0,0): F = (0,-1,172/837,0,0), G = (21801/256,0,174676879/1285632,0,0); (0,1): F = (0,-1,0,0,0), G = (-215215/2232,0,0,0,0); (1,0): F = (0,-1,17522973/732224,-32041321/8878216,0), G = (148733/39060,0,36560277/138880,-174676879/4399920,0); (1,1): F = (0,-1,-149769/9424,0,0), G = (5434/873,0,-3437291/18042,0,0); (1,2): F = (0,-1,0,0,0), G = (-1540/279,0,0,0,0); (2,0): [F = (0,-1,187652/962109,6994767/36453241,1033591/36453241), G = (15286843/1901200,0,10123374287/91257600,-4062253/218736,-1572091911/471497600)] + [F = (0,0,0,-1,-45389295/297856639), G = (0,0,23064254926472539/925970646585600,0,-180544450042489/1594727224675200)]; (2,1): F = (0,-1,-17329/24732,48074/117477,0), G = (-13053/2170,0,-138073/2520,312481/9765,0); (2,2): F = (0,-1,-43/9,0,0), G = (1,0,559/12,0,0).\n\nInterpretation: the count of bracket determinants is polynomial in (lambda1, lambda2) and tracks |Lambda| (5, 7, 11 generic; 4, 5, 9 reduced for |Lambda| = 3, 4, 5), not dim V (8, 15, 15). In every wedge the vectors vanish on the first point m = -1-lambda1 or beyond the support of the column (for F), all numbers are exact rationals.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Reach table at finite twist, exact, no untwisting (Task 6)\n\nP_phys^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3 Gauss decomposition without pivoting, exact); x0^(1) = e1 rho(U0); the undone site-1 covector of a rotation g is e1 rho(g L0 D0) (D0 only rescales components). For a generic rotation (4 points) and for 4 rational points of every genuine locus component of Task 4/5 (cell 24): the weights of V reached (nonzero components), the rank of the stacked undone covectors on every weight space, against the slice weights nu - Lambda needed for Lambda x Lambda (nu = highest weights of the 225 (64) states, from the kernels of E12_tot, E23_tot per weight sector; required rank = multiplicity of nu).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 6: reach table at finite twist (exact, no untwisting). P_phys^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (Gauss decomposition without pivoting, 3x3), x0^(1) = e1 rho(U0); the undone site-1 covector of a rotation g is e1 rho(g L0 D0). Weights of V reached and rank on every weight space, against the slice weights nu - Lambda of the highest-weight states nu of Lambda x Lambda. *)\nee3[i_, j_] := Table[KroneckerDelta[i, ii] KroneckerDelta[j, jj], {ii, 3}, {jj, 3}];\nzq = zN;\nPpp3 = MatrixExp[(1/zq[[1]]) ee3[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[-(1/(zq[[1]] zq[[2]])) ee3[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[((zq[[1]] + zq[[2]])/(zq[[1]] zq[[2]])) ee3[2, 3]];\nPmp3 = MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[1]] ee3[3, 2]] . MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[2]] ee3[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[3]] ee3[2, 1]];\nP3 = Pmp3 . DiagonalMatrix[sVec[zq]] . Ppp3; P3inv = Inverse[P3];\nMg = P3inv; l21 = Mg[[2, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[2]] = Mg[[2]] - l21 Mg[[1]]; l31 = Mg[[3, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l31 Mg[[1]]; l32 = Mg[[3, 2]]/Mg[[2, 2]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l32 Mg[[2]];\nL0 = {{1, 0, 0}, {l21, 1, 0}, {l31, l32, 1}}; D0 = Diagonal[Mg]; U0 = Inverse[DiagonalMatrix[D0]] . Mg;\nrhoLow[L_] := nexp[L[[2, 1]] Ee[2, 1]] . nexp[L[[3, 1]] Ee[3, 1]] . nexp[L[[3, 2]] Ee[3, 2]];\nrhoUp[U_] := nexp[U[[1, 2]] Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[(U[[1, 3]] - U[[1, 2]] U[[2, 3]]) Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[U[[2, 3]] Ee[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3, exact)\"] = (L0 . DiagonalMatrix[D0] . U0 === P3inv);\nchecks[\"rho(P^-1) = rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) on V (exact)\"] = zeroM[SparseArray[PphInv1] - rhoLow[L0] . ρdiag[D0] . rhoUp[U0]];\nchecks[\"e1 rho(P^-1) = rho(D0)_11 e1 rho(U0) (exact)\"] = (e1 . PphInv1 == ρdiag[D0][[1, 1]] (e1 . rhoUp[U0]));\nundone[pt_] := Normal[e1 . nexp[pt[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[pt[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[pt[[3]] Ee[2, 3]] . rhoLow[L0] . ρdiag[D0]];\n(* weights of V with multiplicities; highest-weight states of Lambda x Lambda (kernel of E12tot, E23tot on each weight sector) and the slice weights nu - Lambda *)\nwV = Union[wtL1]; multV = Association[Table[w -> Count[wtL1, w], {w, wV}]];\nE12t = E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2]; E23t = E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3];\nhwMult = Association[Table[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]]}, mu -> Length[NullSpace[Join[Normal[E12t[[All, sec]]], Normal[E23t[[All, sec]]]]]]], {mu, Union[wtBasis]}]];\nhwNu = Select[hwMult, # > 0 &];\nslice = Association[KeyValueMap[#1 - Λ -> #2 &, hwNu]];\nchecks[\"# HW states, # irreps in Lambda x Lambda\"] = {Total[hwNu], Length[hwNu]};\nchecks[\"every slice weight is a weight of V\"] = SubsetQ[wV, Keys[slice]];\n(* sample points: generic rotations and, for every genuine locus found in Task 4, up to 3 rational points *)\ngenPts = {{1, 2, 3}, {1/2, 1/3, 2}, {2, -1, 1/2}, {-3/2, 2/5, 3}};\nfamilies = Join[{{\"generic rotation\", genPts}}, Table[{\"locus \" <> ToString[Factor /@ c[[1]], InputForm] <> \" (dim \" <> ToString[c[[2]]] <> \")\", c[[3]]}, {c, compTab}]];\n(* a point is only listed if it is a genuine rotation: all of gA gB gC nonzero (guaranteed by ratPoints) *)\nreachOf[pts_] := Module[{us = undone /@ pts, idxW},\n  Table[With[{ix = Flatten[Position[wtL1, w]]}, {w, multV[w], If[KeyExistsQ[slice, w], slice[w], 0], MatrixRank[us[[All, ix]]]}], {w, wV}]];\n{tims[\"reach table\"], reachTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[fam[[1]] -> reachOf[fam[[2]]], {fam, families}]]];\n(* summary per family: weights reached, whether every required slice weight is reached with the required rank, ranks on multi-dimensional weight spaces *)\nfamSummary[name_] := Module[{rt = reachTab[name]}, {name, Length[Select[rt, #[[4]] > 0 &]], Length[wV], And @@ (#[[4]] >= #[[3]] & /@ rt), Select[rt, #[[2]] > 1 &][[All, {1, 2, 4}]]}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"L0, D0, U0\", {L0, D0, U0}}, {\"checks: LDU, rho(P^-1), e1 rho(P^-1)\", {checks[\"P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3, exact)\"], checks[\"rho(P^-1) = rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) on V (exact)\"], checks[\"e1 rho(P^-1) = rho(D0)_11 e1 rho(U0) (exact)\"]}}, {\"weights of V: {weight, multiplicity}\", {#, multV[#]} & /@ wV}, {\"HW weights nu of Lambda x Lambda (multiplicity)\", Normal[hwNu]}, {\"slice weights nu - Lambda (required rank)\", Normal[slice]}, {\"# HW states, # irreps\", checks[\"# HW states, # irreps in Lambda x Lambda\"]}}, {{\"family: {name, # weights reached, # weights of V, all slice weights reached with full rank?, {weight, mult, rank} on multi-dim weight spaces}\", \"\"}}, Table[{#[[1]], Rest[#]} &[famSummary[fam[[1]]]], {fam, families}], {{\"sample points\", \"\"}}, Table[{fam[[1]], fam[[2]]}, {fam, families}], {{\"time (s)\", tims[\"reach table\"]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 6 results (exact; z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3), same for all reps: L0 = {{1,0,0},{-23/12,1,0},{5/6,-2/3,1}}, D0 = diag(1,-1/4,35/72), U0 = {{1,1,1},{0,1,10/3},{0,0,1}})\n\nExact checks (all reps): P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3) True; rho(P^-1) = rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) on V (exact) True; e1 rho(P^-1) = rho(D0)_11 e1 rho(U0) (rho(D0)_11 = 1) True.\n\n| rep | weights of V (multiplicity > 1) | HW states nu of Lambda x Lambda (multiplicity) | slice weights nu - Lambda (required rank) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [2,1,0] | 7 weights; (1,1,1) x2 | 6 HW states over 5 weights: (4,2,0), (4,1,1), (3,3,0), (3,2,1) x2, (2,2,2) | (2,1,0), (2,0,1), (1,2,0), (1,1,1) [2], (0,1,2) |\n| [3,1,0] | 12 weights; (1,1,2), (1,2,1), (2,1,1) x2 | 10 HW states over 8 weights: (6,2,0), (6,1,1), (5,3,0), (5,2,1) x2, (4,4,0), (4,3,1) x2, (4,2,2), (3,3,2) | (3,1,0), (3,0,1), (2,2,0), (2,1,1) [2], (1,3,0), (1,2,1) [2], (1,1,2), (0,2,2) |\n| [3,2,0] | 12 weights; (1,2,2), (2,1,2), (2,2,1) x2 | 10 HW states over 8 weights: (6,4,0), (6,3,1), (6,2,2), (5,5,0), (5,4,1) x2, (5,3,2) x2, (4,4,2), (4,3,3) (the 8 weights have multiplicities 1,1,1,1,2,2,1,1) | (3,2,0), (3,1,1), (3,0,2), (2,3,0), (2,2,1) [2], (2,1,2) [2], (1,2,2), (1,1,3) |\n\n(The [3,1,0] data agree with `L2-310-untwist-CG.md` section 2: 10 HW states in 8 irreps.)\n\n| rep | family (4 rational points each) | weights reached / weights of V | all slice weights reached with the required rank? | rank on the double weight spaces |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [2,1,0] | generic rotation | 7 / 7 | True | (1,1,1): 2 |\n| [2,1,0] | quadric 43 gA^2 = 16 (gB + gA gC) (genuine, dim 2) | 7 / 7 | True | (1,1,1): 2 |\n| [3,1,0] | generic rotation | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,1,0] | gA^2 = gB + gA gC (dim 2) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,1,0] | 3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2 = 0 (dim 2) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,1,0] | 39 gA^2 = 4 (gB + gA gC) (dim 2) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,1,0] | curve {243 gB = 280 gC^2, 351 gA = 140 gC} (dim 1) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,2,0] | generic rotation | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,2,0] | 117 gA^2 gB - 86 gB^2 - 43 gA gB gC + 43 gA^2 gC^2 = 0 (dim 2) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,2,0] | curve {1247689 gB = 461332 gC^2, 1117 gA = -194 gC} (dim 1) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,2,0] | 39 gA^2 = 8 (gB + gA gC) (dim 2) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n| [3,2,0] | curve {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC} (dim 1) | 12 / 12 | True | all three: 2 |\n\nSample points: generic (1,2,3), (1/2,1/3,2), (2,-1,1/2), (-3/2,2/5,3); locus points as listed in the Task 5 table (cell 26) (4 points each; [3,1,0] gA^2 = gB + gA gC: (-3,3,-2), (-3,6,-1), (-3,12,1), (-3,15,2); [2,1,0] quadric: (4,23,5), (4,27,4), (4,31,3), (4,35,2)). Time 0.004-0.03 s per rep.\n\nResult: every genuine locus found (including all reduced-bracket loci and the 1-dimensional curves) reaches ALL weights of V with full rank (2 on every doubly degenerate weight space) with 4 rational points, hence all required slice weights: the families are CG-complete at finite twist, exactly as the adjoint quadric. Because the reach is already complete at the weight level, the weight table does not discriminate between the reduced loci; the discrimination is the bracket count (Task 5).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
