  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Structure of the closed-form measures on the locus: (i) which minor slots of each column vanish identically, (ii) the support of every F and G over the points m (a single point = delta function), (iii) the degrees of the entries in (gA, gC), (iv) whether a gauge exists in which a wedge vector is independent of (gA, gC): the column space of the antisymmetric matrix of a column (the plane spanned by F, G for a rank-2 column; the 4-dim image for the rank-4 column) must contain a vector common to all parameter values; the common subspace is computed exactly as the null space of the stacked annihilators at random rational points of the locus and then re-verified at further points. *)\nslotsOn[c2_, c_] := Table[{mnL[[i]], colLoc[c2, c][[i]] =!= 0}, {i, nMin}];\nnzSlots[c2_, c_] := Select[slotsOn[c2, c], Last][[All, 1]];\nzeroSlots[c2_, c_] := Select[slotsOn[c2, c], Not[Last[#]] &][[All, 1]];\nsuppOf[v_] := mPts[[Flatten[Position[v, x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]];\nentDeg[e_] := With[{tt = Together[e]}, {Exponent[Numerator[tt], gA], Exponent[Numerator[tt], gC], Exponent[Denominator[tt], gA], Exponent[Denominator[tt], gC]}];\nvecDeg[v_] := Max /@ Transpose[entDeg /@ Select[v, # =!= 0 &]];\nvecVars[v_] := Union[Cases[v, gA | gC, {-1}]];\nSeedRandom[17];\nrndPts[n_] := Table[{gA -> RandomChoice[{-1, 1}] RandomInteger[{1, 9}]/RandomInteger[{1, 4}], gC -> RandomChoice[{-1, 1}] RandomInteger[{1, 9}]/RandomInteger[{1, 5}]}, {n}];\ncvPts = rndPts[10]; cvPts2 = rndPts[6];\ncommonVecs[c2_, c_, pts_] := With[{cons = Join @@ Table[NullSpace[amat[colLoc[c2, c]] /. pt], {pt, pts}]}, If[cons === {}, IdentityMatrix[pPts], NullSpace[cons]]];\ncvecs = Association[Flatten[Table[{c2, c} -> commonVecs[c2, c, cvPts], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1]];\ncvOK[c2_, c_] := And @@ Flatten[Table[Dot[nv, v] === 0, {pt, cvPts2}, {nv, NullSpace[amat[colLoc[c2, c]] /. pt]}, {v, cvecs[{c2, c}]}]];\ncvecCheck = Association[Flatten[Table[{c2, c} -> cvOK[c2, c], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1]];\nstrucTab = Flatten[Table[{{c2, c}, \"nonzero minor slots\", nzSlots[c2, c], \"identically zero minor slots\", zeroSlots[c2, c], \"wedges: {pivot, supp F, supp G, degrees (num gA, num gC, den gA, den gC) of F, of G, variables of F, of G}\", Map[{#[[1]], suppOf[#[[2]]], suppOf[#[[3]]], vecDeg[#[[2]]], vecDeg[#[[3]]], vecVars[#[[2]]], vecVars[#[[3]]]} &, cfDec[{c2, c}]], \"delta-function measures (single-point support)\", Select[Flatten[Map[{{#[[1]], \"F\", suppOf[#[[2]]]}, {#[[1]], \"G\", suppOf[#[[3]]]}} &, cfDec[{c2, c}]], 1], Length[#[[3]]] == 1 &], \"common vectors of the column space over the whole locus (basis; {} = none), verified at 6 further points\", {cvecs[{c2, c}], cvecCheck[{c2, c}]}}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1];\nGrid[Prepend[Flatten[Map[Function[r, {{\"(c2, c) = \" <> ToString[r[[1]]], \"\"}, {r[[2]], r[[3]]}, {r[[4]], r[[5]]}, {r[[6]], r[[7]]}, {r[[8]], r[[9]]}, {r[[10]], r[[11]]}}], strucTab], 1], {\"quantity\", \"value\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6b-3 results: structure of the closed-form measures\n\nMinor slots are (n, n') with n < n', points m as above. \"Support\" = points m where the vector is nonzero. All of this is read off the closed forms of 6b-1 (exact).\n\n**[3,1,0]** (locus gB + gA gC = gA^2)\n\n| (c2, c) | nonzero minor slots of the column | identically zero slots | wedges: supp F, supp G | degrees in (gA, gC): numerator (gA, gC) / denominator (gA, gC) of F; of G | variables in F; G |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (0,0) | (-4,-3), (-4,-2), (-3,-2), (-4,-1), (-3,-1), (-2,-1) | all (n, 0) | {-3,-2,-1}; {-4,-3,-2} | F: (1,1)/(3,1); G: (6,1)/(0,0) | gA, gC; gA, gC |\n| (0,1) | (-4,-3), (-4,-2), (-3,-2) | (n,-1), (n,0) | {-3,-2}; {-4,-2} | F: (1,0)/(0,0); G: (3,0)/(0,0) | gA; gA |\n| (1,0) | all except (-1,0) (9 slots) | (-1,0) | w1: {-3,-2,-1,0}; {-4,-3,-2}. w2: {-1}; {-3,-2} | w1 F: (1,1)/(4,1); G: (6,1)/(0,0). w2 F: constant; G: (5,1)/(0,0) | w1: gA, gC; gA, gC. w2: none; gA, gC |\n| (1,1) | (-4,-3), (-4,-2), (-3,-2), (-4,-1), (-3,-1), (-2,-1) | all (n, 0) | {-3,-2,-1}; {-4,-2,-1} | F: (2,0)/(0,0); G: (3,0)/(0,0) | gA; gA |\n\n**[2,1,0]** (quadric)\n\n| (c2, c) | nonzero slots | identically zero slots | supp F; supp G | degrees num/den of F; of G | variables |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (0,0) | (-3,-2), (-3,-1), (-2,-1) | all (n, 0) | {-2,-1}; {-3,-2} | F: (1,1)/(2,1); G: (4,1)/(0,0) | gA, gC; gA, gC |\n| (0,1) | (-3,-2) | all others | {-2}; {-3} | F: constant; G: (1,0)/(0,0) | none; gA |\n| (1,0) | all except (-1,0) | (-1,0) | {-2,-1,0}; {-3,-2} | F: (1,1)/(3,1); G: (4,1)/(0,0) | gA, gC; gA, gC |\n| (1,1) | (-3,-2), (-3,-1), (-2,-1) | all (n, 0) | {-2,-1}; {-3,-1} | F: (1,0)/(0,0); G: (2,0)/(0,0) | gA; gA |\n\nObservations.\n- **Delta functions** (single-point support): [3,1,0]: only wedge 2 of the vacuum column, F = -delta_{m=-1} (G is supported on {-3,-2}); [2,1,0]: column (0,1) is a pure product of two delta functions, F = -delta_{m=-2}, G = (-3395 gA/1674) delta_{m=-3}. Everything else has support on 2 to 4 points.\n- **Degrees:** every entry is a Laurent monomial in gA times at most one factor linear in (gA, gC) in the numerator and the single factor (gA - gC) = beta/alpha (adjoint: (43 gA - 16 gC) = 16 beta/alpha) in the denominator; the G vectors are polynomials (degree up to 6 in gA, 1 in gC); the poles of F sit only at gA = 0 and beta = 0, i.e. on the excluded non-genuine set. Columns c = 1 ((0,1) and (1,1), both reps) depend on gA ONLY (gamma drops out of the whole column on the locus: `Variables` of the [3,1,0] columns is {gA}; for [2,1,0] read off F, G); the c = 0 columns depend on both.\n- **Gauge independent of (gA, gC)?** Exact test: the column space of the antisymmetric matrix of the column (= span{F, G} for a rank-2 column, 4-dim image for the rank-4 one) is intersected over 10 random rational points of the locus (null space of the stacked annihilators) and re-checked at 6 more points. **[3,1,0]: the intersection is {0} for all four columns, so there is NO gauge in which F or G is independent of (gA, gC)** (in the present gauge F and G of the c = 1 columns depend on gA only, those of the c = 0 columns on gA and gC). **[2,1,0]: only column (0,1): the plane is the constant plane spanned by e_{m=-3}, e_{m=-2} (the common vectors are exactly these two basis vectors), so F = -e_{-2} constant with all the (gA) dependence in the amplitude of G (G = -3395 gA/1674 e_{-3}); for the other three columns the intersection is {0}.**",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Natural-measure test. Can a wedge vector X (F or G, per column, on the locus) be written X_m = wgt(m) rho^m (p + q m) on the support points S of the column, wgt(m) = 1/prod_{m' in S, m' != m} (m' - m) h, with (rho, p, q) functions of (gA, gC)? With r_m = X_m/wgt(m): r_m rho^(-m) must be linear in m. For S = consecutive integers this means the second differences vanish: r_(m+1) - 2 rho r_m + rho^2 r_(m-1) = 0 for every interior m. k = |S| = 2: always solvable (trivially, 3 unknowns for 2 numbers); k = 3: one quadratic in rho (always solvable over the algebraic closure; rho is a rational function iff the discriminant is a perfect square); k = 4, 5: the quadratics must have a common root: pairwise resultants in rho must vanish identically. Exact (Together/Factor/Resultant, 120 s each). Also tested: whether the PLANE span{F, G} of a rank-2 column contains a natural vector (k = 3: always, a 1-parameter family; k = 4: the 4x4 determinant of {F, G, n1(rho), n2(rho)} on S vanishes for some rho). *)\ncolSupport[c2_, c_] := Select[Range[pPts], AnyTrue[amat[colLoc[c2, c]][[#]], # =!= 0 &] &];\nwgtS[S_, m_] := 1/Product[(mm - m) hN, {mm, DeleteCases[mPts[[S]], m]}];\ntf[x_] := With[{r = TimeConstrained[Factor[Together[x]], 120, $Failed]}, If[r === $Failed, cfStall = True; x, r]];\nstripRho[p_] := If[p === 0, 0, Expand[p/rho1^Exponent[p, rho1, Min]]];\nnatTest[Xv_, S_] := Module[{k = Length[S], rv, polys, sols, res},\n  If[Not[Union[Differences[mPts[[S]]]] === {1}], Return[{\"support not consecutive\", mPts[[S]]}]];\n  If[k <= 2, Return[{\"trivially yes (|S| <= 2)\", mPts[[S]]}]];\n  rv = tf /@ (Xv[[S]]/Table[wgtS[S, m], {m, mPts[[S]]}]);\n  (* second differences of r_m rho^(-m), cleared of powers of rho (rho = 0 is not an admissible root) *)\n  polys = DeleteCases[stripRho /@ Table[Numerator[Together[rv[[i + 2]] - 2 rho1 rv[[i + 1]] + rho1^2 rv[[i]]]], {i, k - 2}], 0];\n  If[polys === {}, Return[{\"all second differences vanish: any rho\", rv}]];\n  If[Length[polys] == 1,\n   sols = Quiet[Solve[polys[[1]] == 0, rho1]];\n   Return[{\"k = 3, one condition: rho =\", Factor /@ (rho1 /. sols), \"rho rational in (gA, gC)?\", FreeQ[sols, _Root | _Complex | Power[_, Rational[_, 2]]], \"r\", rv}]];\n  res = Table[tf[Resultant[polys[[a]], polys[[b]], rho1]], {a, Length[polys]}, {b, a + 1, Length[polys]}];\n  {If[AllTrue[Flatten[res], # === 0 &], \"common nonzero root exists: YES\", \"common nonzero root: NO (resultants nonzero)\"], {\"resultants\", Flatten[res]}}];\nnatTab = Flatten[Table[With[{S = colSupport[c2, c]}, Table[{{c2, c}, mPts[[S]], wedgeIdx, name, natTest[If[name === \"F\", cfDec[{c2, c}][[wedgeIdx, 2]], cfDec[{c2, c}][[wedgeIdx, 3]]], S]}, {wedgeIdx, Length[cfDec[{c2, c}]]}, {name, {\"F\", \"G\"}}]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 3];\n(* plane test for rank-2 columns with |S| = 4: some natural vector in span{F, G}? determinant of {F, G, n1(rho), n2(rho)} with n1 = wgt rho^m, n2 = wgt m rho^m on S *)\nplaneTest[c2_, c_] := Module[{S = colSupport[c2, c], dec = cfDec[{c2, c}], k, nv1, nv2, det4},\n  k = Length[S];\n  If[Length[dec] =!= 1, Return[\"rank 4 column: image 4-dim, a natural vector exists trivially (dimension count)\"]];\n  If[k <= 3, Return[\"|S| <= 3: a natural vector in the plane exists for every rho (dimension count)\"]];\n  If[Union[Differences[mPts[[S]]]] =!= {1}, Return[\"support not consecutive\"]];\n  nv1 = Table[wgtS[S, m] rho1^m, {m, mPts[[S]]}]; nv2 = Table[wgtS[S, m] m rho1^m, {m, mPts[[S]]}];\n  det4 = tf[Numerator[Together[Det[{dec[[1, 2, S]], dec[[1, 3, S]], nv1, nv2}]]]];\n  If[k == 4, {\"4x4 determinant (numerator), degree in rho1, # irreducible factors over Q(gA, gC)\", det4, Exponent[det4, rho1], Length[FactorList[det4]] - 1 - Count[FactorList[det4][[2 ;;, 1]], _?(FreeQ[#, rho1] &)]}, \"|S| = 5 not needed\"]];\nplaneTab = Flatten[Table[{{c2, c}, planeTest[c2, c]}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1];\nGrid[Join[{{\"(c2, c)\", \"support points S\", \"wedge #\", \"F or G\", \"natural-measure test\"}}, natTab, {{\"plane test (rank-2 columns): does span{F, G} contain a natural vector?\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}, Map[{#[[1]], \"\", \"\", \"\", #[[2]]} &, planeTab]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6b-4 results: natural-measure test  X_m = wgt(m) rho^m (p + q m),  wgt(m) = 1/prod_{m' != m}(m' - m) h over the support S of the column  (report, not forced)\n\nMethod (exact): r_m = X_m/wgt(m) must make r_m rho^(-m) linear in m, i.e. r_(m+1) - 2 rho r_m + rho^2 r_(m-1) = 0 for all interior m of S (rho = 0 is excluded: powers of rho are divided out; my first version let rho = 0 count as a common root and gave a spurious \"yes\" for G of the adjoint (1,0), fixed). |S| = 3: one condition (always solvable over the algebraic closure); |S| = 4, 5: the quadratics must have a common nonzero root, tested with pairwise `Resultant` in rho (nonzero resultant = no solution (rho, p, q) as functions of (gA, gC)). Whether the PLANE span{F, G} contains a natural vector was tested as well (4x4 determinant of {F, G, n1(rho), n2(rho)} on S for |S| = 4).\n\n| rep, (c2, c), S | F | G |\n|---|---|---|\n| [3,1,0] (0,0), S = {-4..-1} | **no** (resultant 311364 gA^2 (3179 gA - 3675 gC)(2 gA - 3 gC)^2 != 0) | **no** (resultant -15732297393750 gA^13 (gA - gC)^3 != 0) |\n| [3,1,0] (0,1), S = {-4,-3,-2} | **yes, rational:** rho = -4 gA/9, p = -64 gA^3/729, q = -16 gA^3/729 (checked exactly at the three points) | only over C: rho = +- i sqrt(86/27) gA (rho^2 = -86 gA^2/27, not a rational function) |\n| [3,1,0] (1,0), S = {-4..0}, wedge 1 | **no** (3 nonzero resultants) | **no** |\n| [3,1,0] (1,0), wedge 2 (F = -delta_{-1}) | no (the delta function is not natural on 5 points) | **no** |\n| [3,1,0] (1,1), S = {-4..-1} | **no** (resultant -643108 gA^2) | **no** (resultant -5493849 gA^6) |\n| [2,1,0] (0,0), S = {-3,-2,-1} | **yes, rational:** rho = 27 gA (43 gA - 16 gC)/(31 (43 gA - 32 gC)) (r_{-3} = 0, so p = 3 q, q = r_{-2} rho^2) | **yes, rational:** rho = -43 gA/54 (r_{-1} = 0) |\n| [2,1,0] (0,1), S = {-3,-2} | trivially yes (|S| = 2: F = -delta_{-2}) | trivially yes (G = (-3395 gA/1674) delta_{-3}) |\n| [2,1,0] (1,0), S = {-3..0} | **no** (resultant 162 gA^2 (27 gA - 62 gC)(3469627 gA^2 - 7161556 gA gC + 2430400 gC^2) != 0) | **no** (resultant -43 gA^3 (43 gA - 16 gC) != 0; no common root other than the excluded rho = 0) |\n| [2,1,0] (1,1), S = {-3,-2,-1} | **yes, rational:** rho = -16 gA/27 | only over C: rho = +- (i/3) sqrt(43/2) gA |\n\nPlane test (span{F, G} contains a natural vector): |S| <= 3 always (dimension count, one-parameter family of rho); [3,1,0] (0,0): the determinant is -70 gA times an **irreducible quartic** in rho with (gA, gC)-dependent coefficients; [3,1,0] (1,1): 4 (1032 gA^4 - 2752 gA^3 rho - 2880 gA^2 rho^2 + 3483 gA rho^3 - 108 rho^4), i.e. rho = kappa gA with kappa a root of the **irreducible quartic** 108 kappa^4 - 3483 kappa^3 + 2880 kappa^2 + 2752 kappa - 1032 = 0 (so the plane is spanned by two natural vectors, but rho is not a rational function); [3,1,0] (1,0): the 4-dim image contains a natural vector for every rho (dimension count); [2,1,0] (1,0): **irreducible cubic** in rho.\n\n**Answer.** Natural measures exist only where the support has at most 3 points: [3,1,0] (0,1) F; [2,1,0] (0,0) F and G, (1,1) F (rational rho: these have a zero at an end point of S, which turns the quadratic condition into a linear one), and trivially for the 2-point support. For every column with 4 or 5 support points ((0,0), (1,0), (1,1) of [3,1,0]; (1,0) of [2,1,0]) none of the vectors F, G is of the form wgt rho^m (p + q m) for any (rho, p, q) depending on (gA, gC); the planes contain natural vectors only for rho in the roots of irreducible quartics/cubics. So the measure is NOT a \"natural\" Gauss-Jacobi-type weight on the 4- and 5-point columns; the 3-point cases are three numbers fitted by three unknowns and should not be read as structure.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* t-dependence of the closed-form measures of [3,1,0] (cheap version of Task 7: no z-scan, only (h, theta) points). RUN LAST: this cell wipes Global`* (it re-runs the setup cells with other parameter lines, read from this notebook's own file); every helper and result lives in the context T8`. Afterwards re-run cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19 (and the closed-form cells) to restore the base state. The pivots of the base point are forced at every other point so that F, G are compared in the same gauge. *)\nT8`nbFile = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/gaudin-cg/Paul/Mathematica/new-conventions/L2-site1-rotation-brackets-general.wb\";\nT8`codeCells := T8`codeCells = Select[Import[T8`nbFile, \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"], #[\"kind\"] == 2 &][[All, \"value\"]];\nT8`pick[s_] := First[Select[T8`codeCells, StringContainsQ[#, s] &]];\nT8`seq = {\"the ONLY rep switch\", \"eigenstates of the twisted chain\", \"dual Q's: Q^j(x)\", \"physical-space Gauss factors\", \"untwisted L=2 B(u)\", \"Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule\", \"Task 2: site-1 covectors\", \"Task 3: coefficient tensors\", \"Task 4a\"};\nT8`cfKey = \"Closed-form bracket measures on the locus\";\nT8`run[lam_String, hs_String, ths_String, zs_String, piv_] := (\n  T8`subs = {\"Λ = {2, 1, 0};\" -> \"Λ = \" <> lam <> \";\", \"hN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5}; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3};\" -> \"hN = \" <> hs <> \"; thN = \" <> ths <> \"; zN = \" <> zs <> \";\"};\n  T8`t0 = AbsoluteTime[];\n  Scan[ToExpression[StringReplace[T8`pick[#], T8`subs], InputForm] &, T8`seq];\n  T8`t1 = AbsoluteTime[] - T8`t0;\n  If[piv =!= None, ToExpression[\"Global`cfPivForced = \" <> ToString[piv, InputForm]]];\n  ToExpression[T8`pick[T8`cfKey], InputForm];\n  <|\"t\" -> ToExpression[\"tPar\"], \"dec\" -> ToExpression[\"cfDec\"], \"resid\" -> ToExpression[\"cfResid\"], \"pf\" -> ToExpression[\"pfTab\"], \"K\" -> ToExpression[\"Kg\"], \"tSetup\" -> T8`t1, \"tTotal\" -> AbsoluteTime[] - T8`t0|>);\n(* parameter points: base, then (h, theta) variants (h = 1/2 unless noted) *)\nT8`pts = {{\"base\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\"}, {\"h = 1/3, th = (1/5, -4/9)\", \"1/3\", \"{1/5, -4/9}\"}, {\"th2 = 1/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/5}\"}, {\"th2 = -26/105\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -26/105}\"}, {\"th2 = -27/28\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -27/28}\"}, {\"th2 = -37/42\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -37/42}\"}, {\"th2 = -1/70\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -1/70}\"}, {\"th2 = -3/7\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/7}\"}, {\"th2 = -5/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -5/3}\"}, {\"th2 = 1/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/3}\"}};\nT8`base = T8`run[\"{3, 1, 0}\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\", None];\nT8`piv = Map[#[[All, 1]] &, T8`base[\"dec\"]];\n(* every point under a 150 s guard: the setup at th2 = 3/4 (an earlier choice) stalled for more than 100 s and was replaced by th2 = -5/3 *)\nT8`runSafe[i_] := With[{r = TimeConstrained[AbsoluteTiming[T8`run[\"{3, 1, 0}\", T8`pts[[i, 2]], T8`pts[[i, 3]], \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\", T8`piv]], 150, $Failed]}, If[r === $Failed, Nothing, T8`pts[[i, 1]] -> r[[2]]]];\nT8`res = Association[Prepend[Table[T8`runSafe[i], {i, 2, Length[T8`pts]}], \"base\" -> T8`base]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{k, T8`res[k][\"t\"], T8`res[k][\"resid\"], N[T8`res[k][\"tSetup\"], 3], N[T8`res[k][\"tTotal\"], 3]}, {k, Keys[T8`res]}], {\"point\", \"t = theta12/h\", \"closed-form residual per (c2, c) at this t (0 = decomposition exact on the locus)\", \"setup time (s)\", \"total (s)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* t-dependence analysis of the closed-form measures of [3,1,0] (uses only T8` data; run after the driver cell). (i) the locus gB + gA gC = gA^2 is the same at every t: the closed-form residual vanishes at every t and the Pfaffian generators of the columns (0,0) and (1,1) carry the factor gA^2 - gB - gA gC at every t. (ii) every entry of F and G (same pivots, same gauge) is written as  c(t) gA^a gC^b prod (gA - kappa_i(t) gC)^e_i  (linear forms normalised monic in gA); c(t) and kappa_i(t) are fitted as exact rational functions of t from the sample points (smallest total degree through all points, via the null space of the linear system; at least one point is left as validation). *)\nT8`ts = Table[T8`res[k][\"t\"], {k, Keys[T8`res]}];\nT8`locusFactor[pf_] := FreeQ[Denominator[Together[pf/(gA^2 - gB - gA gC)]], gA | gB | gC];\nT8`locusTab = Table[{k, T8`res[k][\"t\"], {T8`locusFactor[First[T8`res[k][\"pf\"][[1, 1, 4]]]], T8`locusFactor[First[T8`res[k][\"pf\"][[2, 2, 4]]]]}, T8`res[k][\"resid\"]}, {k, Keys[T8`res]}];\n(* the vacuum column (1,0) (5 points, rank <= 4 automatic): its genuine decomposability locus (4x4 Pfaffians saturated by gA gB gC) stays EMPTY at every t *)\nT8`sat10 = Table[GroebnerBasis[Append[T8`res[k][\"pf\"][[2, 1, 4]], 1 - T8`wS gA gB gC], {gA, gB, gC}, {T8`wS}], {k, Keys[T8`res]}];\nT8`sat10Empty = Union[T8`sat10] === {{1}};\n(* prefactors: Pfaffian of (0,0) = c00(t) gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC) (3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2); Pfaffian of (1,1) = c11(t) (gA^2 - gB - gA gC) (cc11(t) gA^2 - gB - gA gC) *)\nT8`c00 = Table[Together[T8`res[k][\"pf\"][[1, 1, 4, 1]]/(gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC) (3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2))], {k, Keys[T8`res]}];\nT8`q11 = Table[Together[T8`res[k][\"pf\"][[2, 2, 4, 1]]/(gA^2 - gB - gA gC)], {k, Keys[T8`res]}];\nT8`cc11 = Table[Coefficient[q, gA, 2]/(-Coefficient[q, gB]), {q, T8`q11}]; T8`c11 = Table[-Coefficient[q, gB], {q, T8`q11}];\nT8`normE[e_] := Module[{tt = Together[e], c = 1, forms = {}, a, b},\n  If[tt === 0, Return[{0, {}}]];\n  Do[Do[With[{f = pr[[1]], ex = sg pr[[2]]},\n     Which[NumberQ[f], c = c f^ex,\n      f === gA || f === gC, AppendTo[forms, {f, ex}],\n      PolynomialQ[f, {gA, gC}] && Exponent[f /. {gA -> s1 gA, gC -> s1 gC}, s1] == 1 && FreeQ[f /. {gA -> 0, gC -> 0}, _?(# =!= 0 &)],\n      a = Coefficient[f, gA]; b = Coefficient[f, gC]; c = c a^ex; AppendTo[forms, {gA + (b/a) gC, ex}],\n      True, AppendTo[forms, {f, ex}]]], {pr, FactorList[If[sg == 1, Numerator[tt], Denominator[tt]]][[2 ;;]]}], {sg, {1, -1}}];\n  c = c FactorList[Numerator[tt]][[1, 1]]/FactorList[Denominator[tt]][[1, 1]];\n  {c, SortBy[forms, ToString]}];\nT8`ratFitN[ts_, vals_] := Module[{res = {}, ns, tt = T8`tv},\n  Do[If[res === {} && m + n + 2 <= Length[ts] - 1,\n    ns = NullSpace[Table[Join[Table[ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, m}], Table[-vals[[i]] ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, n}]], {i, Length[ts]}]];\n    If[Length[ns] == 1, res = Factor[(Sum[ns[[1, k + 1]] tt^k, {k, 0, m}])/(Sum[ns[[1, m + 2 + k]] tt^k, {k, 0, n}])]]], {tot, 0, 8}, {m, 0, tot}, {n, 0, tot - m}]; res];\n(* entry laws: per (column, wedge, vector, point index) *)\nT8`keys = Keys[T8`res];\nT8`entryLaw[colKey_, w_, vi_, idx_] := Module[{data = Table[T8`normE[T8`res[k][\"dec\"][colKey][[w, vi + 1, idx]]], {k, T8`keys}], cs, fm, const, varF, kapFits, cFit},\n  If[AllTrue[data[[All, 1]], # === 0 &], Return[0]];\n  If[Length[Union[Length /@ data[[All, 2]]]] =!= 1, Return[{\"form count changes with t\", data}]];\n  cs = data[[All, 1]]; fm = data[[All, 2]];\n  (* forms: same (form, exponent) at all t -> constant; otherwise (non-constant kappa) treat position-wise by exponent *)\n  const = Intersection @@ fm;\n  varF = Table[Complement[f, const], {f, fm}];\n  If[Length[Union[Length /@ varF]] =!= 1, Return[{\"form structure changes\", data}]];\n  kapFits = If[varF[[1]] === {}, {}, Table[With[{exps = varF[[All, j, 2]], kaps = varF[[All, j, 1]]}, If[Length[Union[exps]] == 1 && AllTrue[kaps, PolynomialQ[# - gA, {gA, gC}] &], {T8`ratFitN[T8`ts, Coefficient[#, gC] & /@ kaps], exps[[1]]}, {\"unmatched\", varF[[All, j]]}]], {j, Length[varF[[1]]]}]];\n  cFit = T8`ratFitN[T8`ts, cs];\n  {cFit, Join[const, kapFits]}];\nT8`npts = Length[T8`res[\"base\"][\"dec\"][{0, 0}][[1, 2]]]; T8`ptsM = Range[-T8`npts + 1, 0];\nT8`laws = Association[Flatten[Table[{ck, w, vname, idx} -> T8`entryLaw[ck, w, If[vname === \"F\", 1, 2], idx], {ck, Keys[T8`res[\"base\"][\"dec\"]]}, {w, Length[T8`res[\"base\"][\"dec\"][ck]]}, {vname, {\"F\", \"G\"}}, {idx, T8`npts}], 3]];\n(* the fitted law as an expression in t (T8`tv) and (gA, gC): c(t) prod forms; a form whose first entry does not contain gA, gC is a fitted kappa(t): (gA + kappa gC)^e *)\nT8`lawExpr[law_] := If[law === 0, 0, law[[1]] Times @@ Table[If[FreeQ[f[[1]], gA | gC], (gA + f[[1]] gC)^f[[2]], f[[1]]^f[[2]]], {f, law[[2]]}]];\nT8`lawOK = AllTrue[Flatten[Table[With[{dec = T8`res[k][\"dec\"], tv = T8`res[k][\"t\"]}, Table[Together[(T8`lawExpr[T8`laws[{ck, w, vn, idx}]] /. T8`tv -> tv) - dec[ck][[w, If[vn === \"F\", 2, 3], idx]]] === 0, {ck, Keys[dec]}, {w, Length[dec[ck]]}, {vn, {\"F\", \"G\"}}, {idx, T8`npts}]], {k, Keys[T8`res]}]], TrueQ];\nT8`lawRows = KeyValueMap[Function[{key, law}, If[law === 0, Nothing, {key[[1]], key[[2]], key[[3]], T8`ptsM[[key[[4]]]], T8`lawExpr[law] /. T8`tv -> t}]], T8`laws];\n(* the assembled closed form of the measures for [3,1,0] on gB + gA gC = gA^2, as functions of (t, gA, gC): {(c2, c)} -> list of wedges {F, G} over the points m = -4..0, pivots (1,4); (1,2); (1,5),(2,4); (1,2); gauge F_i = 0, F_j = -1, G_j = 0. Checked against the stored decomposition at every sampled t. *)\nT8`hand[tt_, a_, g_] := <|{0, 0} -> {{{0, -tt (2 a - 3 g)/(3 (tt - 2) a^2 (a - g)), 2 tt (2 a - 3 g)/(3 (tt - 1) a (a - g)), -1, 0}, {-3 a^3 (a - g)/tt, 6 (tt - 3) a^4 (a - g)/(tt (tt - 2)), -3 (tt - 3) a^5 (a - g)/(tt (tt - 1)), 0, 0}}}, {0, 1} -> {{{0, -1, 3 (tt - 2) a/(2 (tt - 1)), 0, 0}, {-2 (tt + 1) a/(tt (tt - 2)), 0, 4 (tt - 3) (tt + 1) a^3/(tt (tt - 1) (tt - 2)), 0, 0}}}, {1, 0} -> {{{0, ((tt - 1) a - tt g)/((tt - 3) a^3 (a - g)), -((3 tt - 2) a - 3 tt g)/((tt - 2) a^2 (a - g)), tt (2 a - 3 g)/((tt - 1) a (a - g)), -1}, {-(tt - 3) a^3 (a - g)/tt, 3 (tt - 3) a^4 (a - g)/tt, -3 (tt - 3) a^5 (a - g)/tt, 0, 0}}, {{0, 0, 0, -1, 0}, {0, a^3 (a - g), -3 (tt - 3) a^4 (a - g)/(tt - 2), 0, 0}}}, {1, 1} -> {{{0, -1, 3 (tt - 3) a/(tt - 2), -3 (tt - 3) a^2/(tt - 1), 0}, {1, 0, -2 (3 tt - 10) a^2/(tt - 2), 8 (tt - 3) a^3/(tt - 1), 0}}}|>;\nT8`handOK = And @@ Flatten[Table[With[{h = T8`hand[T8`res[k][\"t\"], gA, gC], d = T8`res[k][\"dec\"]}, Table[Together[h[ck][[w, vi]] - d[ck][[w, vi + 1]]] === ConstantArray[0, T8`npts], {ck, Keys[d]}, {w, Length[d[ck]]}, {vi, 2}]], {k, Keys[T8`res]}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"all fitted laws reproduce the stored closed forms at every sampled t (exact); the assembled closed form T8`hand does too\", {T8`lawOK, T8`handOK}, \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"# t values, t values\", Length[T8`ts], T8`ts, \"\", \"\"}, {\"locus: factor gA^2 - gB - gA gC in the Pfaffians of (0,0) and (1,1) at every t; residual of the closed form zero at every t\", {T8`locusTab[[All, 3]] // Union, T8`locusTab[[All, 4]] // Union}, \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"genuine part of column (1,0) empty at every t\", T8`sat10Empty, \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"Pfaffian prefactors: c00(t) (column (0,0)), c11(t) and cc11(t) (column (1,1)), fitted\", {T8`ratFitN[T8`ts, T8`c00] /. T8`tv -> t, T8`ratFitN[T8`ts, T8`c11] /. T8`tv -> t, T8`ratFitN[T8`ts, T8`cc11] /. T8`tv -> t}, \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"(c2, c)\", \"wedge\", \"F or G\", \"point m\", \"entry = c(t) prod form^e  (t = theta12/h)\"}}, T8`lawRows], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6b-5 / 6b-6 results: t-dependence of the [3,1,0] closed forms (cheap version; the driver 6b-5 re-runs cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19 and 6b-1 for each (h, theta) line; z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3) throughout; WIPES Global`)\n\nRequested point: h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9), t = 29/15 (setup 18 s in a busy kernel, 7.4 s fresh, 13.6 s in the final driver run; 6b-1 itself 0.02 s with the base pivots forced). Because two values cannot fix a function of t, nine more points were sampled (7.3-7.6 s each when run one at a time in a fresh kernel; 13.6-14.7 s each, 142 s for the whole driver cell, when the driver cell itself was run from the saved notebook text): theta2 = 1/5, -26/105, -27/28, -37/42, -1/70, -3/7, -5/3, 1/3 at h = 1/2, i.e. t = 62/35 (base), 29/15, 6/35, 16/15, 5/2, 7/3, 3/5, 10/7, 82/21, -2/21 (10 values). [A point theta2 = 3/4 tried first stalled in the setup for more than 100 s and was replaced by -5/3; reason not investigated.] After the runs the kernel was restored to the base (h = 1/2, theta = (2/7, -3/5)) state by re-running the setup (the kernel had to be restarted once because of the stalled run).\n\n**1. The locus is t-independent.** The closed-form residual (sum of wedges - column, exact) is 0 for all four columns at all 10 values of t with the SAME locus gB + gA gC = gA^2 (b2^2 = b1 b3); the Pfaffian generators of the columns (0,0) and (1,1) contain the factor gA^2 - gB - gA gC at every t. Locus polynomials at t = 29/15 (recomputed, InputForm):\n- (0,0): `{(5400*gB*(gA^2 - gB - gA*gC)*(3*gA^2*gB - gB^2 + gA*gB*gC + 2*gA^2*gC^2))/203}`\n- (1,1): `{(-48*(gA^2 - gB - gA*gC)*(31*gA^2 - gB - gA*gC))/7}`\n- (1,0) (five 4x4 Pfaffians; the genuine part, saturated by gA gB gC, is EMPTY at t = 29/15 and at every sampled t, Groebner basis {1}): `{(16*gA^2*gB^2*(31*gA^2 - 24*gB - 24*gA*gC))/203, (-768*gA*gB^2*(8*gA^2 - gB - gA*gC)*(gB + gA*gC))/203, (48*gB^2*(353*gA^2 - 24*gB - 24*gA*gC)*(gB + gA*gC)^2)/203, (-48*gB*(gA^2 - gB - gA*gC)*(-450*gA*gB + 449*gA^2*gC - 29*gB*gC - 29*gA*gC^2))/841, (8*(1736*gA^4*gB - 2918*gA^2*gB^2 + 1392*gB^3 - 1568*gA^3*gB*gC + 1434*gA*gB^2*gC - 1347*gA^4*gC^2 + 1476*gA^2*gB*gC^2 - 87*gB^2*gC^2 + 1434*gA^3*gC^3 - 174*gA*gB*gC^3 - 87*gA^2*gC^4))/203}`\n\nExact t-laws of the prefactors (fitted on 10 values, exact): Pf(0,0) = 3 (t-3)/(t (t-1)(t-2)) gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2) (everything but the prefactor t-independent); Pf(1,1) = 6 (t-3)/(t-1) (gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(cc gA^2 - gB - gA gC) with **cc = (t-4)/(t-2)** (the t-dependent conic of Task 7, 39/4 at t = 62/35, 31 at 29/15).\n\n**2. The measures at t = 29/15** (same pivots, same gauge; InputForm):\n- (0,0): `F = {0, (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(3*gA^2*(gA - gC)), (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(21*gA*(gA - gC)), -1, 0}`, `G = {(-45*gA^3*(gA - gC))/29, (1440*gA^4*(gA - gC))/29, (360*gA^5*(gA - gC))/203, 0, 0}`\n- (0,1): `F = {0, -1, (-3*gA)/28, 0, 0}`, `G = {(1320*gA)/29, 0, (21120*gA^3)/203, 0, 0}`\n- (1,0): wedge 1 `F = {0, -1/16*(14*gA - 29*gC)/(gA^3*(gA - gC)), (3*(19*gA - 29*gC))/(gA^2*(gA - gC)), (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(14*gA*(gA - gC)), -1}`, `G = {(16*gA^3*(gA - gC))/29, (-48*gA^4*(gA - gC))/29, (48*gA^5*(gA - gC))/29, 0, 0}`; wedge 2 `F = {0, 0, 0, -1, 0}`, `G = {0, gA^3*(gA - gC), -48*gA^4*(gA - gC), 0, 0}`\n- (1,1): `F = {0, -1, 48*gA, (24*gA^2)/7, 0}`, `G = {1, 0, -126*gA^2, (-64*gA^3)/7, 0}`\n\nSame structure (supports, zero patterns, the delta F of wedge 2, degrees) at both t; only the numerical coefficients and the t-dependent linear forms change.\n\n**3. Closed form in t (exact on all 10 sampled t; every entry is c(t) x gA-monomial x (gA - gC)^+-1 x linear forms; every c(t) and every linear-form slope is a rational function with numerator degree <= 2 and denominator degree <= 3, found as the lowest-degree exact fit through all 10 points, so each is over-determined).** On gB = gA^2 - gA gC, points m = -4..0, same pivots/gauge, t = theta12/h:\n- (0,0): `F = {0, -t (2 gA - 3 gC)/(3 (t-2) gA^2 (gA - gC)), 2 t (2 gA - 3 gC)/(3 (t-1) gA (gA - gC)), -1, 0}`, `G = {-3 gA^3 (gA - gC)/t, 6 (t-3) gA^4 (gA - gC)/(t (t-2)), -3 (t-3) gA^5 (gA - gC)/(t (t-1)), 0, 0}`\n- (0,1): `F = {0, -1, 3 (t-2) gA/(2 (t-1)), 0, 0}`, `G = {-2 (t+1) gA/(t (t-2)), 0, 4 (t-3)(t+1) gA^3/(t (t-1)(t-2)), 0, 0}`\n- (1,0): wedge 1 `F = {0, ((t-1) gA - t gC)/((t-3) gA^3 (gA - gC)), -((3t-2) gA - 3 t gC)/((t-2) gA^2 (gA - gC)), t (2 gA - 3 gC)/((t-1) gA (gA - gC)), -1}`, `G = {-(t-3) gA^3 (gA - gC)/t, 3 (t-3) gA^4 (gA - gC)/t, -3 (t-3) gA^5 (gA - gC)/t, 0, 0}`; wedge 2 `F = {0, 0, 0, -1, 0}`, `G = {0, gA^3 (gA - gC), -3 (t-3) gA^4 (gA - gC)/(t-2), 0, 0}`\n- (1,1): `F = {0, -1, 3 (t-3) gA/(t-2), -3 (t-3) gA^2/(t-1), 0}`, `G = {1, 0, -2 (3t-10) gA^2/(t-2), 8 (t-3) gA^3/(t-1), 0}`\n\nThese reproduce the stored closed forms exactly at every sampled t (checks in 6b-6: `T8`lawOK`, `T8`handOK`: True, True) and at t = 62/35 and 29/15 give the lists of 6b-1 and item 2 (e.g. (0,1): F_{-2} = -4 gA/9 and -3 gA/28, G_{-4} = 3395 gA/248 and 1320 gA/29). All coefficients are rational functions of t with poles only at t in {0, 1, 2, 3} (the integer values of t = theta12/h at which ladder-1 and ladder-2 points coincide); the slopes of the t-dependent linear forms are t/(t-1) ((1,0), F_{-3}) and 3t/(3t-2) ((1,0), F_{-2}); (2 gA - 3 gC) and (gA - gC) are t-independent.\n\nAnswer to \"how do the coefficients change\": the locus and the pivot/gauge structure do not change; the measure coefficients are the short rational functions of t listed above (two values alone would not fix them; the ten-point fit does, exactly).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6c. u-structure of the bracket measures of the [3,1,0] family (added 2026-10-10, later session; Paul's request)\n\nQuestion: the closed forms of 6b (cell 41) are pairs (F, G) per wedge, gauge dependent. The invariant of a column (c2, c) is the 2-form A^(c2,c) = sum over its wedges of F^G, (F^G)_{mm'} = F_m G_m' - F_m' G_m, on the points m = -4..0 (x_m = theta1 + m h); the column is Bk2[F, G] for any F, G in the plane P = Im A (rank 2), resp. a sum of two such for the rank-4 column (1,0). Setting as in 6b: [3,1,0] on gB + gA gC = gA^2 (no t in the locus), t = theta12/h, s := gC/gA. \"Five columns\" = the five wedges: (0,0), (0,1), (1,0) [two wedges], (1,1). All statements exact (Together/Factor/NullSpace/Groebner over Q(gA, s, t)); the Groebner solves are over (s, t) and took well under a second (the 120 s guard was never hit, no numeric fallback).\n\nHow evaluated: like the rest of this notebook, from the saved cell sources in the shared kernel K1 (VS Code does not open this file); every code cell below was run from exactly its saved text. 6c-1 .. 6c-4 need the base [3,1,0] state (cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19, the 6b-1 cell and the cell 33 definitions bk2N, cfOverlapDev). The driver 6c-5 WIPES Global` (it re-runs the setup cells for the adjoint at ten (h, theta) points and for [3,1,0] at h = 1/3); run it last, then restore the base state and re-run 6c-1, 6c-2, 6c-3 before 6c-5b and 6c-6 (6c-6 needs the helper definitions of 6c-2 and 6c-3, 6c-5b those of 6c-1 and 6c-3). Notation: m-frame = h = 1, theta1 = 0 (p a polynomial in u is a polynomial in m of the same degree; the weights are products of linear factors in m and t).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 6c-1: the gauge-invariant kernel A^(c2,c) = sum over the wedges of a column of F^G, (F^G)_{mm'} = F_m G_m' - F_m' G_m, assembled from the t-closed forms of 6b-5 (cell 41). Setting: [3,1,0], locus gB + gA gC = gA^2, points m = -4..0 (index 1..5), h-independent in the variable t = theta12/h. Requires the base [3,1,0] state (cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19 and the 6b-1 cell for colMat). The F, G pairs are gauge dependent (pivot gauge), A is not. *)\nClearAll[uHand, uWed, uA, uPts, uExp, uKern, uKernList, uP29];\nuPts = {-4, -3, -2, -1, 0};\nuHand[tv_, a_, g_] := <|{0, 0} -> {{{0, -tv (2 a - 3 g)/(3 (tv - 2) a^2 (a - g)), 2 tv (2 a - 3 g)/(3 (tv - 1) a (a - g)), -1, 0}, {-3 a^3 (a - g)/tv, 6 (tv - 3) a^4 (a - g)/(tv (tv - 2)), -3 (tv - 3) a^5 (a - g)/(tv (tv - 1)), 0, 0}}}, {0, 1} -> {{{0, -1, 3 (tv - 2) a/(2 (tv - 1)), 0, 0}, {-2 (tv + 1) a/(tv (tv - 2)), 0, 4 (tv - 3) (tv + 1) a^3/(tv (tv - 1) (tv - 2)), 0, 0}}}, {1, 0} -> {{{0, ((tv - 1) a - tv g)/((tv - 3) a^3 (a - g)), -((3 tv - 2) a - 3 tv g)/((tv - 2) a^2 (a - g)), tv (2 a - 3 g)/((tv - 1) a (a - g)), -1}, {-(tv - 3) a^3 (a - g)/tv, 3 (tv - 3) a^4 (a - g)/tv, -3 (tv - 3) a^5 (a - g)/tv, 0, 0}}, {{0, 0, 0, -1, 0}, {0, a^3 (a - g), -3 (tv - 3) a^4 (a - g)/(tv - 2), 0, 0}}}, {1, 1} -> {{{0, -1, 3 (tv - 3) a/(tv - 2), -3 (tv - 3) a^2/(tv - 1), 0}, {1, 0, -2 (3 tv - 10) a^2/(tv - 2), 8 (tv - 3) a^3/(tv - 1), 0}}}|>;\nuWed[F_, G_] := Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, 5}, {j, 5}];\nuA[tv_, a_, g_][key_] := Together /@ Total[uWed @@@ uHand[tv, a, g][key], {1}];\n(* (i) exact: assembled A equals the direct tensor colMat (the antisymmetric matrix of colLoc) at t = 62/35, symbolic in (gA, gC) *)\nuChk62 = Table[Together[uA[tPar, gA, gC][{c2, c}] - colMat[c2, c]] === ConstantArray[0, {5, 5}], {c2, 0, 1}, {c, 0, 1}];\n(* (ii) t = 29/15: the closed forms against the stored lists printed in cell 41 (those were verified against the direct tensors at h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9) in 6b-5; the direct tensors there are re-built in the driver of 6c-5) *)\nuP29 = <|{0, 0} -> {{{0, (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(3*gA^2*(gA - gC)), (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(21*gA*(gA - gC)), -1, 0}, {(-45*gA^3*(gA - gC))/29, (1440*gA^4*(gA - gC))/29, (360*gA^5*(gA - gC))/203, 0, 0}}}, {0, 1} -> {{{0, -1, (-3*gA)/28, 0, 0}, {(1320*gA)/29, 0, (21120*gA^3)/203, 0, 0}}}, {1, 0} -> {{{0, -1/16*(14*gA - 29*gC)/(gA^3*(gA - gC)), (3*(19*gA - 29*gC))/(gA^2*(gA - gC)), (29*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(14*gA*(gA - gC)), -1}, {(16*gA^3*(gA - gC))/29, (-48*gA^4*(gA - gC))/29, (48*gA^5*(gA - gC))/29, 0, 0}}, {{0, 0, 0, -1, 0}, {0, gA^3*(gA - gC), -48*gA^4*(gA - gC), 0, 0}}}, {1, 1} -> {{{0, -1, 48*gA, (24*gA^2)/7, 0}, {1, 0, -126*gA^2, (-64*gA^3)/7, 0}}}|>;\nuChk29 = Table[Union[Flatten[Together[uHand[29/15, gA, gC][k] - uP29[k]]]] === {0}, {k, Keys[uP29]}];\n(* (iii) the gA-power law: with gC = sR gA, A_{mm'} = gA^(m + m' + uExp[c2,c]) a_{mm'}(sR, tv), a free of gA *)\nuExp = <|{0, 0} -> 9, {0, 1} -> 8, {1, 0} -> 8, {1, 1} -> 7|>;\nuKern = Association[Table[k -> Association[Table[{uPts[[i]], uPts[[j]]} -> Factor[Together[uA[tv, gA, sR gA][k][[i, j]]/gA^(uPts[[i]] + uPts[[j]] + uExp[k])]], {i, 5}, {j, i + 1, 5}]], {k, Keys[uExp]}]];\nuKernFree = FreeQ[Values /@ Values[uKern], gA];\n(* the exponent is forced: the lowest power of gA in every nonzero entry equals m + m' + uExp *)\nuExpCheck = Table[Union[Table[With[{e = Factor[uA[tv, gA, sR gA][k][[i, j]]]}, If[e === 0, Nothing, Exponent[Numerator[e], gA, Min] - Exponent[Denominator[e], gA, Min] - uPts[[i]] - uPts[[j]]]], {i, 5}, {j, i + 1, 5}] // Flatten], {k, Keys[uExp]}];\nuKernList = Association[Table[k -> Select[Normal[uKern[k]], #[[2]] =!= 0 &], {k, Keys[uExp]}]];\nGrid[{{\"A (closed forms) = direct colMat at t = 62/35, exact, (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1)\", Flatten[uChk62]}, {\"closed forms = stored lists at t = 29/15\", uChk29}, {\"gA-free residual kernels (all four)\", uKernFree}, {\"gA exponent offset per column (single value each; law m + m' + 9 - c2 - c)\", uExpCheck}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6c-1 results: the gA-power law and the residual kernels (item 1)\n\nChecks (all exact): (i) the assembled A = sum F^G of the t-closed forms equals the direct tensor colMat (antisymmetric matrix of colLoc) at t = 62/35 identically in (gA, gC) for all four columns (True x 4); (ii) at t = 29/15 the closed forms equal the stored lists of cell 41 (True x 4) AND the direct tensors rebuilt at h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9) by the driver (cell 6c-5b: True x 4); (iii) with gC = s gA every nonzero entry is exactly gA^(m+m'+c) a_{mm'}(s, t) with a free of gA (True), c read off as the lowest gA-power minus m - m' (a single value per column). Time 0.25 s.\n\n**Exponent law.** A^(c2,c)_{mm'} = gA^(m + m' + 9 - c2 - c) a^(c2,c)_{mm'}(s, t), s = gC/gA, i.e. gA^((u + u' - 2 theta1)/h) x gA^(9 - c2 - c): the gA-dependence is a pure exponential in u + u', the constant IS column dependent (9, 8, 8, 7 for (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1)) and drops by one for each of c2 and c. The gC-dependence is homogeneous (a function of s only) and AFFINE in s ((0,0) and (1,0) carry s; (0,1) and (1,1) do not). Entries not listed are zero ((n, 0) slots of (0,0), (1,1); (n, -1), (n, 0) of (0,1); (-1, 0) of (1,0)).\n\n**Residual kernels a_{mm'}(s, t)** (Factor-ed, InputForm, pairs m < m'; t = theta12/h; poles only at t in {0, 1, 2}; the (1,0) kernel is the total of its two wedges):\n\n- `(c2, c) = (0, 0)`: `<|{-4, -3} -> (-2+3*s)/(-2+t), {-4, -2} -> (-2*(-2+3*s))/(-1+t), {-4, -1} -> (3*(-1+s))/t, {-3, -2} -> (3*(-2+3*s)*(-3+t))/((-2+t)*(-1+t)), {-3, -1} -> (-6*(-1+s)*(-3+t))/((-2+t)*t), {-2, -1} -> (3*(-1+s)*(-3+t))/((-1+t)*t)|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (0, 1)`: `<|{-4, -3} -> (-2*(1+t))/((-2+t)*t), {-4, -2} -> (3*(1+t))/((-1+t)*t), {-3, -2} -> (-4*(-3+t)*(1+t))/((-2+t)*(-1+t)*t)|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (1, 0)`: `<|{-4, -3} -> -((1-t+s*t)/t), {-4, -2} -> ((-3+t)*(2-3*t+3*s*t))/((-2+t)*t), {-4, -1} -> -(((-2+3*s)*(-3+t))/(-1+t)), {-4, 0} -> ((-1+s)*(-3+t))/t, {-3, -2} -> (-3*(-4+8*t-7*s*t-2*t^2+2*s*t^2))/((-2+t)*t), {-3, -1} -> (17-26*s-5*t+8*s*t)/(-1+t), {-3, 0} -> (-3*(-1+s)*(-3+t))/t, {-2, -1} -> (-3*(-3+t)*(3-5*s-t+2*s*t))/((-2+t)*(-1+t)), {-2, 0} -> (3*(-1+s)*(-3+t))/t|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (1, 1)`: `<|{-4, -3} -> 1, {-4, -2} -> (-3*(-3+t))/(-2+t), {-4, -1} -> (3*(-3+t))/(-1+t), {-3, -2} -> (2*(-10+3*t))/(-2+t), {-3, -1} -> (-8*(-3+t))/(-1+t), {-2, -1} -> (6*(-3+t))/(-1+t)|>`\n\n(E.g. a^(0,0)_{-4,-3} = (3s - 2)/(t - 2); the whole block on {-4,-3,-2} of (0,0) carries the common factor (3s - 2), the entries with m' = -1 the factor (s - 1).)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
