  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6c-3 results: explicit F(u), G(u) for the columns with a class structure (item 3)\n\n(0,1) and the end-point-modified (0,0) work; (1,0) and (1,1) do not (item 2).\n\n**(0,1)** (3-point support S3 = {-4,-3,-2}, P = wgt3 Pol_1 / (m (t + m + 1))). With P3(u) = (u - theta1 + 2h)(u - theta1 + 3h)(u - theta1 + 4h) (wgt3(x_m) = 1/P3'(x_m) on the nodes u = theta1 - 2h, -3h, -4h):\n\n    F(u) = h^4 gA^((u-theta1)/h) / ( P3'(u) (u - theta1) (u - theta2 + h) ),     G(u) = h^3 gA^((u-theta1)/h) / ( P3'(u) (u - theta2 + h) ),\n    A^(0,1) = lam01 gA^8 F^G,   lam01 = 48 (t-3)(t+1)/t,\n\nso the (0,1) contribution to the overlap is lam01 gA^8 Bk2[F, G] Q^3(theta1 - h) with <Q^j F>_1 = sum over the three nodes (a Lagrange divided difference of Q^j(u) gA^((u-theta1)/h)/(u - theta2 + h) over the 3 nodes, with and without the factor 1/(u - theta1)). In m-units F_m = gA^m wgt3(m)/(m (t+m+1)), G_m = gA^m wgt3(m)/(t+m+1). Exact wedge identity (symbolic in gA, gC at t = 62/35, and symbolic in t, s in the m-frame) and, at the second t (h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9), t = 29/15) against the direct tensors in 6c-5b: True.\n\n**(0,0)** (4-point support S4 = {-4..-1}; P = wgt4 Pol_1/nu, nu = t + m + 1 at m = -4, -3, -2 and nu(-1) = t/om1, om1 = 3(s-1)/(3s-2)). With P4(u) = prod_{n=1..4}(u - theta1 + n h) (wgt4 = -1/P4' on the nodes):\n\n    F(u) = - h^4 gA^((u-theta1)/h) om(u) / ( P4'(u) (u - theta2 + h) ),   G(u) = F(u) (u - theta1)/h,   om(u) = 1 except om(theta1 - h) = om1,\n    A^(0,0) = lam00 gA^9 F^G,   lam00 = -12 (t-3)(3 gC/gA - 2).\n\nSo the column is natural (gA^m wgt4 Pol_1/(t + m + 1)) up to ONE rescaling of the end-point component m = -1 by the s-dependent constant om1 = 3 (gC - gA)/(3 gC - 2 gA). Equivalent form without the anomaly: A^(0,0) = -12 (t-3) gA^(9+m+m') kappa_{mm'}(s) (m'-m) wgt4(m) wgt4(m')/((t+m+1)(t+m'+1)) with kappa = 3s - 2 for pairs not containing m = -1 and 3(s-1) for pairs containing it (checked in 6c-4, True). Exact wedge identities at t = 62/35 (symbolic in gA, gC) and symbolic in t, s: True, True; at t = 29/15, h = 1/3 against the direct tensors: True.\n\n**Overlap identity on all 225 states** (<Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> M1_vac = sum_c2 lam2^(c2) sum_wedges Bk2[F, G] Q^3(theta1 - c h); the other columns are the cell 41 closed forms, the replaced columns are the u-function forms F(u), G(u) above evaluated on the support nodes), relative deviation max|lhs - rhs|/max|lhs| at two fresh rational points of the locus (bigfloat zeros of the stated accuracy, i.e. deviations below 10^-accuracy):\n\n| | 6b forms | (0,1) as F(u), G(u) | (0,0) as F(u), G(u) | both |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (gA, gC) = (5/2, -3/7) | < 10^-45.5 | < 10^-45.5 | < 10^-45.4 | < 10^-45.4 |\n| (gA, gC) = (-4/3, 2/5) | < 10^-47.0 | < 10^-46.9 | < 10^-46.9 | < 10^-46.8 |\n\n(five wedges in all cases; time 1.0 s.) For (1,0) and (1,1) no F(u), G(u) of the tested classes exists, see 6c-2 and 6c-4.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 6c-4: closed-form structure of the kernels. (i) (0,0): A = -12 (tv - 3) gA^(9 + m + m') kappa_{mm'}(sR) (m' - m) w4(m) w4(m') / ((tv + m + 1)(tv + m' + 1)) on S4 = {-4..-1}, kappa = 3 sR - 2 for pairs not containing -1 and 3 (sR - 1) for pairs containing -1 (checked in 6c-3 as uSplit00); (ii) (1,1): A = (tv - 3) gA^(7 + m + m')/((tv + m)(tv + m')) (v ^ (tv x + y)) with the t-independent integer vectors v = (0, 1, -3, 3, 0), x = (-1, 0, 6, -8, 0), y = (4, 0, -20, 24, 0); v = -6 w1(m) on m = -3, -2, -1 where w1(m) = 1/prod_{n=0..3, n != -m}(m + n) is the ladder-1 part of the global SoV measure (its m = 0 value is cut off by the support); (iii) pole scan: for which per-point cross-ladder factors (tv + m + n_m) (n_m in {none, 0..3}) are all entries of D A D polynomial in tv, at sR = 3/7 (minimal total degree first). *)\nuVv = {0, 1, -3, 3, 0}; uXx = {-1, 0, 6, -8, 0}; uYy = {4, 0, -20, 24, 0};\nuChk11 = Union[Flatten[Together[uAm0[{1, 1}] - Table[(tv - 3)/((tv + uPts[[i]]) (tv + uPts[[j]])) (uVv[[i]] (tv uXx[[j]] + uYy[[j]]) - uVv[[j]] (tv uXx[[i]] + uYy[[i]])), {i, 5}, {j, 5}]]]];\nuW1 = Table[1/Product[m + n, {n, DeleteCases[Range[0, 3], -m]}], {m, {-3, -2, -1}}];\nuVvRatio = uVv[[2 ;; 4]]/uW1;\nuChk00 = Union[Flatten[Together[uAm0[{0, 0}] + 12 (tv - 3) Table[If[MemberQ[uS4, uPts[[i]]] && MemberQ[uS4, uPts[[j]]], If[uPts[[i]] == -1 || uPts[[j]] == -1, 3 (sR - 1), 3 sR - 2] (uPts[[j]] - uPts[[i]]) uWm[uS4, uPts[[i]]] uWm[uS4, uPts[[j]]]/((tv + uPts[[i]] + 1) (tv + uPts[[j]] + 1)), 0], {i, 5}, {j, 5}]]]];\nuPoleScan[k_] := Module[{A = uAm0[k] /. sR -> 3/7, best = {}},\n  Scan[Function[ch, Module[{fac = Table[If[ch[[i]] === None, 1, tv + uPts[[i]] + ch[[i]]], {i, 5}], B},\n     B = Table[Together[A[[i, j]] fac[[i]] fac[[j]]], {i, 5}, {j, 5}];\n     If[AllTrue[Flatten[B], PolynomialQ[#, tv] &], AppendTo[best, {Total[Exponent[#, tv] & /@ Select[Flatten[B], # =!= 0 &]], ch}]]]], Tuples[Join[{None}, Range[0, 3]], 5]];\n  Take[SortBy[best, First], UpTo[3]]];\n{uTimePole, uPole} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[k -> uPoleScan[k], {k, {{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}}}]];\nGrid[{{\"(1,1) pencil identity: residual values (0 = exact)\", uChk11}, {\"v / w1 on m = -3, -2, -1\", uVvRatio}, {\"(0,0) closed form residual\", uChk00}, {\"pole scan: best cross-ladder factor choices per column (degree, n_m for m = -4..0)\", uPole}, {\"time (s)\", uTimePole}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6c-4 results: best partial structure for (1,1) and (1,0), pole pattern\n\nTime 19 s (the pole scan: 5^5 factor choices x 4 columns).\n\n- **(1,1)** (never natural, Moebius determinant -24 (t-1)(t-2)(t-3)): the kernel is a t-LINEAR PENCIL of decomposable forms with a common vector. A^(1,1)_{mm'} = (t-3) gA^(m+m'+7)/((t+m)(t+m')) (v^(t x + y))_{mm'} with the t-independent integer vectors v = (0, 1, -3, 3, 0), x = (-1, 0, 6, -8, 0), y = (4, 0, -20, 24, 0) on m = -4..0 (exact, residual 0). The common vector is the ladder-1 part of the SoV measure with the point m = 0 cut off by the support: v = -6 w1(m) on m = -3, -2, -1, w1(m) = 1/prod_{n=0..3, n != -m}(m + n) (the 1, -3, 3 of the pattern 1, -3, 3, -1; v/w1 = {-6, -6, -6}), zero at m = -4 (not a pole of ladder 1) and m = 0. So F_m = gA^m v_m/(t+m) (the four-pole ladder-1 measure, truncated, over the cross factor u - theta2) IS a nice vector; the partner G = gA^m (t x + y)_m/(t+m) (defined mod v) is not of the tested classes. Cross-ladder pole pattern of the entries: 1/(t+m) at m = -2, -1 only (pole scan, degree 12: factors (t+m) at m = -2, -1, 0).\n- **(0,0)**: A (t+m+1)(t+m'+1)/(t-3) is t-INDEPENDENT (affine in s); pole scan: factors (t+m+1) at m = -3, -2, -1 (degree 6); closed form in 6c-3.\n- **(0,1)**: A = (48 (t-3)(t+1)/t) gA^(8+m+m') wgt3(m) wgt3(m') (m'-m)/(m m' (t+m+1)(t+m'+1)): the t-dependence is a scalar times the cross factors 1/((t+m+1)(t+m'+1)) (the scan finds no purely polynomial form because of the scalar 1/t).\n- **(1,0)** (rank 4): no per-point cross-ladder factor (t + m + n) makes all entries polynomial in t (poles at t = 0, 1, 2 in a mixed pattern: (-4,-3), (-4,0), (-3,0), (-2,0): 1/t; (-4,-2), (-3,-2): 1/(t(t-2)); (-4,-1), (-3,-1): 1/(t-1); (-2,-1): 1/((t-2)(t-1))); the plane contains delta_{-1} and one vector on every pair of points; the annihilator n = (s-1)(m+1)((t-5)m-6)/2 + e_0 has the non-factorising linear factor (t-5)m - 6.\n- **t-pole pattern per entry (all four columns):** poles only at t in {0, 1, 2}; the factor (t-3) occurs in most entries; (0,1) carries the overall (t+1).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 6c-5 driver: direct column tensors for the adjoint on its quadric at ten (h, theta) points, and for [3,1,0] at the h = 1/3 point (t = 29/15). RUN LAST: it wipes Global` (it re-runs the setup cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19 read from this notebook's own file with a substituted parameter line); everything lives in the context U6`. The antisymmetric matrix colMat[c2, c] of every column on the locus gB + gA gC = ccLoc gA^2 is stored (it is gauge free, so no pivot forcing is needed). Afterwards re-run the setup cells (and 6c-1 ... 6c-3) to restore the base [3,1,0] state. *)\nU6`nbFile = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/gaudin-cg/Paul/Mathematica/new-conventions/L2-site1-rotation-brackets-general.wb\";\nU6`codeCells := U6`codeCells = Select[Import[U6`nbFile, \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"], #[\"kind\"] == 2 &][[All, \"value\"]];\nU6`pick[str_] := First[Select[U6`codeCells, StringContainsQ[#, str] &]];\nU6`seq = {\"the ONLY rep switch\", \"eigenstates of the twisted chain\", \"dual Q's: Q^j(x)\", \"physical-space Gauss factors\", \"untwisted L=2 B(u)\", \"Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule\", \"Task 2: site-1 covectors\", \"Task 3: coefficient tensors\", \"Task 4a\"};\nU6`run[lam_String, hs_String, ths_String] := (\n  U6`t0 = AbsoluteTime[];\n  U6`subs = {\"Λ = {2, 1, 0};\" -> \"Λ = \" <> lam <> \";\", \"hN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5}; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3};\" -> \"hN = \" <> hs <> \"; thN = \" <> ths <> \"; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3};\"};\n  Scan[ToExpression[StringReplace[U6`pick[#], U6`subs], InputForm] &, U6`seq];\n  ToExpression[\"Global`ccLoc = If[Global`Λ === {3, 1, 0}, 1, (Global`tPar - 3)/(2 (Global`tPar - 2))]; Global`locRule = Global`gB -> Ccl Global`gA^2 - Global`gA Global`gC /. Ccl -> Global`ccLoc; Global`colMat[c2_, c_] := Global`amat[Expand /@ (Global`colS[c2, c] /. Global`locRule)];\", InputForm];\n  <|\"t\" -> ToExpression[\"Global`tPar\"], \"cc\" -> ToExpression[\"Global`ccLoc\"], \"mats\" -> Association[Flatten[Table[{c2, c} -> ToExpression[\"Global`colMat[\" <> ToString[c2] <> \", \" <> ToString[c] <> \"]\"], {c2, 0, 1}, {c, 0, 1}], 1]], \"pts\" -> ToExpression[\"Global`mPts\"], \"time\" -> AbsoluteTime[] - U6`t0|>);\nU6`ths = {{\"base\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\"}, {\"h = 1/3\", \"1/3\", \"{1/5, -4/9}\"}, {\"th2 = 1/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/5}\"}, {\"th2 = -26/105\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -26/105}\"}, {\"th2 = -27/28\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -27/28}\"}, {\"th2 = -37/42\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -37/42}\"}, {\"th2 = -1/70\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -1/70}\"}, {\"th2 = -3/7\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/7}\"}, {\"th2 = -5/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -5/3}\"}, {\"th2 = 1/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/3}\"}};\nU6`safe[lam_, i_] := With[{r = TimeConstrained[U6`run[lam, U6`ths[[i, 2]], U6`ths[[i, 3]]], 150, $Failed]}, If[r === $Failed, Nothing, U6`ths[[i, 1]] -> r]];\n{U6`tAdj, U6`adj} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[U6`safe[\"{2, 1, 0}\", i], {i, Length[U6`ths]}]]];\n{U6`t310, U6`d310} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[U6`safe[\"{3, 1, 0}\", 2]]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{k, U6`adj[k][\"t\"], U6`adj[k][\"cc\"], N[U6`adj[k][\"time\"], 3]}, {k, Keys[U6`adj]}], {\"point (adjoint)\", \"t\", \"locus constant ccLoc\", \"time (s)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 6c-5b: second t-value for [3,1,0] against DIRECT tensors: the driver stored colMat at h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9), t = 29/15 (U6`d310). (i) assembled A from the t-closed forms equals the direct colMat exactly, all four columns; (ii) the u-function forms of 6c-3 (with theta1, theta2, h set to that point) reproduce A^(0,1) and A^(0,0) exactly with the same amplitudes uLam01, uLam00, i.e. the h-powers in F(u), G(u) are right. Needs the base state restored (cells 3-6, ..., 6c-1, 6c-3) after the driver. *)\nuD310 = U6`d310[\"h = 1/3\"];\nuChk29d = Table[Together[uA[uD310[\"t\"], gA, gC][{c2, c}] - uD310[\"mats\"][{c2, c}]] === ConstantArray[0, {5, 5}], {c2, 0, 1}, {c, 0, 1}];\nuU29 = Block[{uX1 = 1/5, uX2 = -4/9, uH = 1/3, tt29 = uD310[\"t\"]},\n  {Together[uD310[\"mats\"][{0, 1}] - uLam01[tt29] gA^8 uWed[uVec[uFu01[gA], uS3], uVec[uGu01[gA], uS3]]] === ConstantArray[0, {5, 5}], Together[uD310[\"mats\"][{0, 0}] - uLam00[gA, gC, tt29] gA^9 uWed[uVec[uFu00[gA, gC], uS4], uVec[uGu00[gA, gC], uS4]]] === ConstantArray[0, {5, 5}]}];\nGrid[{{\"t, h, theta of the stored direct tensors\", {uD310[\"t\"], 1/3, {1/5, -4/9}}}, {\"assembled A = direct colMat at t = 29/15, (0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1), exact\", Flatten[uChk29d]}, {\"u-function forms reproduce A^(0,1), A^(0,0) at h = 1/3\", uU29}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 6c-6: the adjoint [2,1,0] on its quadric: gA-power law, residual kernels a_{mm'}(sR, tv) and the nice-basis tests, from the direct column tensors of the 6c-5 driver (10 values of t, exact). Points m = -3..0 (4 points). The kernels are fitted as rational functions of t from the ten values (lowest total degree, over-determined by at least one point) and the fit is then checked at every point. *)\nClearAll[aEntry, aFit, aKern, aExpOf];\naPts = {-3, -2, -1, 0}; aKeys = Keys[U6`adj]; aTs = Table[U6`adj[k][\"t\"], {k, aKeys}];\naEntry[k_, col_, i_, j_] := Together[U6`adj[k][\"mats\"][col][[i, j]] /. gC -> sR gA];\naExpOf[k_, col_, i_, j_] := With[{e = aEntry[k, col, i, j]}, If[e === 0, Nothing, Exponent[Numerator[e], gA, Min] - Exponent[Denominator[e], gA, Min] - aPts[[i]] - aPts[[j]]]];\naOffsets = Table[Union[Flatten[Table[aExpOf[k, col, i, j], {k, aKeys}, {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]]], {col, {{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}}}];\naExp = AssociationThread[{{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}} -> (First /@ aOffsets)];\naRes[k_, col_, i_, j_] := Together[aEntry[k, col, i, j]/gA^(aPts[[i]] + aPts[[j]] + aExp[col])];\naFreeOfA = And @@ Flatten[Table[FreeQ[aRes[k, col, i, j], gA], {k, aKeys}, {col, Keys[aExp]}, {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]];\naSdeg = Max[Flatten[Table[Exponent[Numerator[aRes[k, col, i, j]], sR], {k, aKeys}, {col, Keys[aExp]}, {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]]];\n(* rational fit in tv through the ten points: lowest total degree, uniquely determined *)\naFit[vals_] := Module[{res = {}, ns},\n  If[AllTrue[vals, # === 0 &], Return[0]];\n  Do[If[res === {} && m + n + 2 <= Length[aTs] - 1, ns = NullSpace[Table[Join[Table[aTs[[i]]^q, {q, 0, m}], Table[-vals[[i]] aTs[[i]]^q, {q, 0, n}]], {i, Length[aTs]}]];\n    If[Length[ns] == 1, res = Factor[(Sum[ns[[1, q + 1]] tv^q, {q, 0, m}])/(Sum[ns[[1, m + 2 + q]] tv^q, {q, 0, n}])]]], {tot, 0, 8}, {m, 0, tot}, {n, 0, tot - m}];\n  If[res === {}, $Failed, res]];\naKernFit = Association[Table[col -> Association[Table[{aPts[[i]], aPts[[j]]} -> Sum[sR^q aFit[Table[Coefficient[aRes[k, col, i, j], sR, q], {k, aKeys}]], {q, 0, aSdeg}], {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]], {col, Keys[aExp]}]];\naFitOK = And @@ Flatten[Table[Together[(aKernFit[col][{aPts[[i]], aPts[[j]]}] /. tv -> U6`adj[k][\"t\"]) - aRes[k, col, i, j]] === 0, {k, aKeys}, {col, Keys[aExp]}, {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]];\naKernList = Association[Table[col -> Select[Normal[aKernFit[col]], #[[2]] =!= 0 &], {col, Keys[aExp]}]];\n(* invariant tests on the fitted kernels (the a-frame matrices of 4 points) *)\naAm[col_] := Table[Which[i == j, 0, i < j, aKernFit[col][{aPts[[i]], aPts[[j]]}], True, -aKernFit[col][{aPts[[j]], aPts[[i]]}]], {i, 4}, {j, 4}];\naRank = Table[MatrixRank[aAm[col] /. {sR -> 3/7, tv -> 11/5}], {col, Keys[aExp]}];\naW4[m_] := 1/Product[mp - m, {mp, DeleteCases[aPts, m]}];\naW6[m_] := 1/(Product[-n - m, {n, DeleteCases[Range[0, 2], -m]}] Product[-tv - n - m, {n, 0, 2}]);\naCross[m_] := 1/Product[tv + m + n, {n, 0, 2}];\naCls[cls_, d_] := Table[Table[Switch[cls, \"a\", aW4[m] uPw[m, k], \"b\", aW6[m] uPw[m, k], \"c\", uPw[m, k], \"d\", aCross[m] uPw[m, k]], {m, aPts}], {k, 0, d}];\naInter[col_, vecs_] := Module[{ns = NullSpace[aAm[col]], sol}, sol = If[ns === {}, {}, NullSpace[Together[ns . Transpose[vecs]]]]; If[sol === {}, {}, Together /@ (sol . vecs)]];\naDims = Table[Length[aInter[col, aCls[cls, d]]], {col, Keys[aExp]}, {cls, {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}}, {d, 0, 2}];\naJump[col_, cls_, d_] := Module[{A = aAm[col], rk, V, r, M, gens},\n  rk = MatrixRank[A /. {sR -> 3/7, tv -> 11/5}]; V = uClearDen /@ aCls[cls, d]; r = rk + d + 1;\n  If[r > 4, Return[\"forced by dimension count\"]];\n  M = Transpose[Join[Transpose[A], V]]; gens = DeleteCases[Union[Numerator /@ Together /@ Flatten[Minors[M, r]]], 0];\n  Factor /@ GroebnerBasis[gens, {sR, tv}]];\naJumps = Association[Flatten[Table[{col, cls, d} -> TimeConstrained[aJump[col, cls, d], 120, $Failed], {col, Keys[aExp]}, {cls, {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}}, {d, 0, 2}], 2]];\naDelta[col_, idx_List] := Module[{ns = NullSpace[aAm[col]], V = Table[UnitVector[4, i], {i, idx}], sol}, sol = NullSpace[Together[ns . Transpose[V]]]; If[sol === {}, {}, Together /@ (sol . V)]];\naDeltas = Table[col -> {Select[Table[{aPts[[i]], aDelta[col, {i}]}, {i, 4}], #[[2]] =!= {} &], Select[Flatten[Table[{aPts[[{i, j}]], aDelta[col, {i, j}]}, {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}], 1], #[[2]] =!= {} &]}, {col, Keys[aExp]}];\naKerOf = Association[Table[col -> (Factor /@ (uClearDen /@ NullSpace[aAm[col]])), {col, Keys[aExp]}]];\naMoeb10 = uMoeb[aKerOf[{1, 0}][[1]], aKerOf[{1, 0}][[2]], {-3, -2, -1, 0}];\nGrid[{{\"gA exponent offsets per column {(0,0),(0,1),(1,0),(1,1)} (single values)\", aOffsets}, {\"gA-free residual kernels; max degree in sR\", {aFreeOfA, aSdeg}}, {\"t values\", aTs}, {\"fitted kernels reproduce the direct tensors at all ten points (exact)\", aFitOK}, {\"ranks of the kernels\", aRank}, {\"dims P cap class (rows columns; classes a,b,c,d; d = 0,1,2)\", aDims}, {\"Moebius determinant of the 4-point column (1,0), nodes -3..0\", aMoeb10}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 6c-5 / 6c-6 results: the adjoint [2,1,0] on its quadric gB + gA gC = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) gA^2 (item 4)\n\nDriver 6c-5: ten (h, theta) points (theta1 = 2/7, theta2 = -3/5 (base), 1/5, -26/105, -27/28, -37/42, -1/70, -3/7, -5/3, 1/3 at h = 1/2, and h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9)), i.e. t = 62/35, 29/15, 6/35, 16/15, 5/2, 7/3, 3/5, 10/7, 82/21, -2/21; adjoint 17 s in total (1.7 s per point), [3,1,0] at h = 1/3 14 s (no stall, no fallback). The gauge-free column matrices colMat were taken directly (no pivot forcing needed); 6c-6 fits every kernel coefficient as a rational function of t through the ten points (lowest total degree, over-determined) and checks the fit exactly at all ten points (True). Time of 6c-6: 1.3 s.\n\n**Exponent law.** A^(c2,c)_{mm'} = gA^(m + m' + 7 - c2 - c) a_{mm'}(s, t), s = gC/gA, points m = -3..0: offsets 7, 6, 6, 5 for (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1) (the [3,1,0] law with 9 -> 7), gA-free (True), affine in s (max degree 1).\n\n**Residual kernels** (t = theta12/h; the quadric constant (t-3)/(2(t-2)) is built in; entries not listed are zero):\n\n- `(c2, c) = (0, 0)`: `<|{-3, -2} -> (2*s)/(-1+t)-(-3+t)/(2*(-2+t)*(-1+t)), {-3, -1} -> (-2*s)/t+(-3+t)/((-2+t)*t), {-2, -1} -> (s*(-3+t))/((-1+t)*t)-(-3+t)^2/(2*(-2+t)*(-1+t)*t)|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (0, 1)`: `<|{-3, -2} -> -((1+t)/((-1+t)*t))|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (1, 0)`: `<|{-3, -2} -> -s+(-1+t)/t, {-3, -1} -> -1/2*(-3+t)/(-1+t)+(2*s*(-2+t))/(-1+t), {-3, 0} -> (-3+t)/(2*t)-(s*(-2+t))/t, {-2, -1} -> (-2*s*(-3+t))/(-1+t)+(-3+t)^2/(2*(-2+t)*(-1+t)), {-2, 0} -> (s*(-3+t))/t-(-3+t)^2/(2*(-2+t)*t)|>`\n- `(c2, c) = (1, 1)`: `<|{-3, -2} -> 1, {-3, -1} -> (-2*(-2+t))/(-1+t), {-2, -1} -> (3*(-3+t))/(2*(-1+t))|>`\n\n**Ranks** of all four kernels: 2. **Class table** (generic dimension of P cap class; classes (a) wgt4, (b) six-pole measure (poles theta_s - n h, n = 0..2), (c) none, (d) cross poles (t+m+n), n = 0..2; d = 0, 1, 2; P is 2-dim in 4-space so d = 2 gives 1 by the dimension count): **all four columns: 0, 0, 1 (forced) for all four classes: no adjoint column is natural in (a)-(d), d <= 1.** Jump loci in the (s, t)-plane (rows with d <= 1 that are not {1}):\n\n```\n{{0, 0}, a, 0} : {(-3 + t)^2, s*(-3 + t), s^2}\n{{0, 0}, a, 1} : {(-3 + t)*(-3 + 4*s + 7*t - 6*s*t - 2*t^2 + 2*s*t^2), s*(-3 + 4*s + 7*t - 6*s*t - 2*t^2 + 2*s*t^2)}\n{{0, 0}, b, 0} : {(-3 + t)^3, s*(-3 + t)^2, s^2*(-3 + t)}\n{{0, 0}, b, 1} : {(-3 + t)^3*(-12 + 16*s + 19*t - 44*s*t + 4*t^2 + 14*s*t^2 - 3*t^3 + 2*s*t^3), s*(-3 + t)^2*(-12 + 16*s + 19*t - 44*s*t + 4*t^2 + 14*s*t^2 - 3*t^3 + 2*s*t^3)}\n{{0, 0}, c, 0} : {(-3 + t)^2, s*(-3 + t), s^2}\n{{0, 0}, c, 1} : {(-3 + t)*(-39 + 52*s + 37*t - 62*s*t - 8*t^2 + 18*s*t^2), s*(-39 + 52*s + 37*t - 62*s*t - 8*t^2 + 18*s*t^2)}\n{{0, 0}, d, 0} : {(-3 + t)^3, s*(-3 + t)^2, s^2*(-3 + t)}\n{{0, 0}, d, 1} : {(-3 + t)^3*(-12 + 16*s + 7*t - 4*s*t + 23*t^2 - 38*s*t^2 - 8*t^3 + 18*s*t^3), s*(-3 + t)^2*(-12 + 16*s + 7*t - 4*s*t + 23*t^2 - 38*s*t^2 - 8*t^3 + 18*s*t^3)}\n{{0, 1}, a, 0} : {(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, a, 1} : {(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, b, 0} : {(-3 + t)*(-2 + t)*(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, b, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(-2 + t)^2*(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, c, 0} : {(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, c, 1} : {(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, d, 0} : {(-3 + t)*(-2 + t)*(1 + t)^2}\n{{0, 1}, d, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(-2 + t)^2*(1 + t)^2}\n{{1, 0}, a, 0} : {-1 + t, -1 + 2*s}\n{{1, 0}, a, 1} : {-1 + t, -1 + 2*s}\n{{1, 0}, b, 0} : {(-3 + t)*(96 - 180*t + 216*t^2 - 133*t^3 + 24*t^4 + t^5), (-3 + t)*(-96 + 64*s + 46*t - 81*t^2 + 26*t^3 + t^4)}\n{{1, 0}, b, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(120 - 96*s - 156*t + 128*s*t + 89*t^2 - 16*s*t^2 - 54*t^3 - 20*s*t^3 + 13*t^4 + 4*s*t^4)}\n{{1, 0}, c, 0} : {-2 - t^2 + t^3, -18 + 28*s - 5*t - 3*t^2}\n{{1, 0}, c, 1} : {14 - 16*s - 45*t + 84*s*t + 28*t^2 - 66*s*t^2 - 5*t^3 + 14*s*t^3}\n{{1, 0}, d, 0} : {(-3 + t)*(-8 + 4*t + 20*t^2 - 9*t^3 + t^4), (-3 + t)*(-20 + 8*s + 29*t - 10*t^2 + t^3)}\n{{1, 0}, d, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(-10 + 8*s + 8*t + 8*s*t + t^2 - 18*s*t^2 + 14*t^3 - 22*s*t^3 - 5*t^4 + 14*s*t^4)}\n{{1, 1}, a, 1} : {-5 + 3*t}\n{{1, 1}, b, 0} : {-3 + t}\n{{1, 1}, b, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(-2 + t)*(-24 + 7*t + 7*t^2)}\n{{1, 1}, c, 1} : {-45 + 19*t}\n{{1, 1}, d, 0} : {-3 + t}\n{{1, 1}, d, 1} : {(-3 + t)^2*(-2 + t)*(-12 - 5*t + 19*t^2)}\n```\n\n**(e)** supports <= 2: (0,0): one vector on each pair of its 3-point support {-3,-2,-1} (e.g. (-2(t-1)/(t-3), 1) on {-3,-2}); (0,1): P = span{e_{-3}, e_{-2}} (the plane IS the span of two deltas: the column is a product of two 1-point bras, F(u), G(u) = gA^((u-theta1)/h) x point evaluations at theta1 - 3h and theta1 - 2h, as found in 6b); (1,0): one vector on {-3,-2}, ((2-t)/(t-3), 1), none on the other pairs; (1,1): one vector on each pair of the 3-point support {-3,-2,-1}: (4(t-2), -3(t-3)) on {-3,-2}, (2(t-1), -3(t-3)) on {-3,-1}, (t-1, -2(t-2)) on {-2,-1}. No single delta except in (0,1). Annihilators: (0,0): `e_0` and `((t-3)q, 2(t-1)q, t(3-8s-t+4st), 0)` with q = 3 - 4s - t + 2st; (0,1): `e_{-1}`, `e_0`; (1,1): `(3(t-3), 4(t-2), 2(t-1), 0)`, `e_0`; (1,0): two (see aKerOf in the cell 6c-6 state). For the one 4-point rank-2 column (1,0) the Moebius determinant is 4 (t-3)(t-2)^3 (t-1) t (1 - t + s t)^2 (3 - 4s - t + 2st)(3 - 8s - t + 4st): zero only on the curves s = (t-1)/t, s = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) (the quadric constant itself) and s = (t-3)/(4(t-2)) (apart from the pole values of t), so P(1,0) is wgt4 Pol_1/nu for some nu only on those curves. The adjoint therefore shows the same picture as [3,1,0]: gA-power law with a column-dependent constant, affine-in-s kernels with poles at t in {0, 1, 2}, no nice basis from the five classes, nice structure only through 2-point vectors; no explicit F(u), G(u) beyond the delta form of (0,1) is claimed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. z-independence and t-dependence (Task 7)\n\nDriver (cell 31, run LAST: it wipes Global`, keeps its helpers in the context T7`, re-reads this notebook's file and re-runs the setup cells up to the loci polynomials with a substituted parameter line). Per rep 8 parameter points: base (h = 1/2, theta = (2/7, -3/5), z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3)), z' = (3/2, 5/4, 3/7) at the same (h, theta), and six more (h, theta) at the base z: theta2 = 1/5, -26/105, -27/28, -37/42, -1/70 (h = 1/2), and (h = 1/3, theta = (1/5, -4/9)) (t = 29/15). Cells 32-34 run the three reps, cell 35 fits the t-dependence of the conic constants cc (gB + gA gC = cc gA^2) per column as Moebius functions (a t + b)/(t + d) on three t values and requires membership in the set of conic constants at the other four t values.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 driver (run LAST, after all other cells: it wipes Global`*, so every helper lives in the context T7` and no Module/Do/Table local of Global` is used across the wipe). Re-reads the setup cells of this notebook, substitutes the parameter line, runs the cells up to the loci polynomials and returns the objects needed for the z-independence and t-dependence tests. T7`nbFile = this notebook. *)\nT7`nbFile = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/gaudin-cg/Paul/Mathematica/new-conventions/L2-site1-rotation-brackets-general.wb\";\nT7`codeCells := T7`codeCells = Select[Import[T7`nbFile, \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"], #[\"kind\"] == 2 &][[All, \"value\"]];\nT7`pick[s_] := First[Select[T7`codeCells, StringContainsQ[#, s] &]];\nT7`seq = {\"the ONLY rep switch\", \"eigenstates of the twisted chain\", \"dual Q's: Q^j(x)\", \"physical-space Gauss factors\", \"untwisted L=2 B(u)\", \"Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule\", \"Task 2: site-1 covectors\", \"Task 3: coefficient tensors\", \"Task 4a\", \"Task 4d\"};\n(* lam: rep as a string such as \"{2, 1, 0}\"; hs, ths, zs: strings; extra: optional expression (string) evaluated in the state reached after the last cell *)\nT7`run[lam_String, hs_String, ths_String, zs_String, extra_String: \"Null\"] := (\n  T7`subs = {\"Λ = {2, 1, 0};\" -> \"Λ = \" <> lam <> \";\", \"hN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5}; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3};\" -> \"hN = \" <> hs <> \"; thN = \" <> ths <> \"; zN = \" <> zs <> \";\"};\n  T7`t0 = AbsoluteTime[];\n  Scan[ToExpression[StringReplace[T7`pick[#], T7`subs], InputForm] &, T7`seq];\n  <|\"t\" -> ToExpression[\"tPar\"], \"K\" -> ToExpression[\"Kg\"], \"pf\" -> ToExpression[\"pfTab\"], \"conic\" -> ToExpression[\"conicTab\"], \"nonConic\" -> ToExpression[\"nonConic\"], \"extra\" -> ToExpression[extra], \"time\" -> AbsoluteTime[] - T7`t0|>);\n(* base point, z' (same h, theta), then other (h, theta) at the base z *)\nT7`pts = {{\"base\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"z'\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 3/7}\"}, {\"th2 = 1/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2 = -26/105\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -26/105}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2 = -27/28\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -27/28}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2 = -37/42\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -37/42}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2 = -1/70\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -1/70}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"h = 1/3, th = (1/5, -4/9)\", \"1/3\", \"{1/5, -4/9}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}};\nT7`repRun[lam_String, which_List] := Association[Map[Function[i, T7`pts[[i, 1]] -> T7`run[lam, T7`pts[[i, 2]], T7`pts[[i, 3]], T7`pts[[i, 4]]]], which]];\n(* summary of a run set: z-independence flags against the base, conic constants cc (gB + gA gC = cc gA^2) per column versus t *)\nT7`summary[res_Association] := Map[Function[k, {k, res[k][\"t\"], If[k == \"z'\", {res[k][\"K\"] === res[\"base\"][\"K\"], res[k][\"pf\"] === res[\"base\"][\"pf\"]}, \"\"], res[k][\"conic\"][[All, {1, 2, 4}]], N[res[k][\"time\"], 3]}], Keys[res]];\nNull",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 run for adjoint (regression): 8 parameter points (base, z-prime, six more (h, theta)); each point re-runs cells up to the loci polynomials. Afterwards Global` holds the LAST parameter point; re-run the notebook from the top to restore the base state. *)\nT7`resA = T7`repRun[\"{2, 1, 0}\", Range[8]];\nGrid[Prepend[T7`summary[T7`resA], {\"point\", \"t = theta12/h\", \"z-prime test: K and Pfaffians identical to the base run?\", \"conic constants {group, column, cc}\", \"time (s)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 run for [3,1,0]: 8 parameter points (base, z-prime, six more (h, theta)); each point re-runs cells up to the loci polynomials. Afterwards Global` holds the LAST parameter point; re-run the notebook from the top to restore the base state. *)\nT7`res310 = T7`repRun[\"{3, 1, 0}\", Range[8]];\nGrid[Prepend[T7`summary[T7`res310], {\"point\", \"t = theta12/h\", \"z-prime test: K and Pfaffians identical to the base run?\", \"conic constants {group, column, cc}\", \"time (s)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 run for [3,2,0]: 8 parameter points (base, z-prime, six more (h, theta)); each point re-runs cells up to the loci polynomials. Afterwards Global` holds the LAST parameter point; re-run the notebook from the top to restore the base state. *)\nT7`res320 = T7`repRun[\"{3, 2, 0}\", Range[8]];\nGrid[Prepend[T7`summary[T7`res320], {\"point\", \"t = theta12/h\", \"z-prime test: K and Pfaffians identical to the base run?\", \"conic constants {group, column, cc}\", \"time (s)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 post-processing: t-dependence of the conic constants cc (gB + gA gC = cc gA^2). Per (group, column) the set of conic constants at each of the 7 distinct t values; every Moebius branch cc(t) = (a t + b)/(t + d) fitted exactly on three t values and required to appear in the set at the other four. Only T7` objects are used (the kernel state of Global` belongs to the last parameter point of the driver). *)\nT7`fitBranches[res_Association, c2_, c_] := Module[{ks = {\"base\", \"th2 = 1/5\", \"th2 = -26/105\", \"th2 = -27/28\", \"th2 = -37/42\", \"th2 = -1/70\", \"h = 1/3, th = (1/5, -4/9)\"}, ts, sets, cand, fits, consts},\n  ts = res[#][\"t\"] & /@ ks;\n  sets = Map[Function[k, Cases[res[k][\"conic\"], {c2, c, _, v_} :> v]], ks];\n  consts = Intersection @@ sets;\n  cand = Tuples[sets[[{1, 2, 3}]]];\n  fits = Flatten[Map[Function[vs, Module[{sol = Quiet[Solve[Thread[vs (ts[[{1, 2, 3}]] + T7`dd) == T7`aa ts[[{1, 2, 3}]] + T7`bb], {T7`aa, T7`bb, T7`dd}]]}, If[sol === {} || Head[sol] =!= List, {}, With[{f = Together[(T7`aa T7`tt + T7`bb)/(T7`tt + T7`dd) /. First[sol]]}, If[AllTrue[Range[4, 7], MemberQ[sets[[#]], Quiet[f /. T7`tt -> ts[[#]]]] &], {f}, {}]]]]], cand], 1];\n  {DeleteDuplicates[fits], consts}];\nT7`fitAll[res_Association] := Table[{{c2, c}, T7`fitBranches[res, c2, c]}, {c2, 0, 2}, {c, 0, 2}];\nT7`fits310 = Select[Flatten[T7`fitAll[T7`res310], 1], #[[2, 1]] =!= {} || #[[2, 2]] =!= {} &];\nT7`fits320 = Select[Flatten[T7`fitAll[T7`res320], 1], #[[2, 1]] =!= {} || #[[2, 2]] =!= {} &];\nT7`fitsAdj = Select[Flatten[T7`fitAll[T7`resA], 1], #[[2, 1]] =!= {} || #[[2, 2]] =!= {} &];\nGrid[{{\"rep\", \"{group, column} -> {Moebius branches cc(t) (a t + b)/(t + d) matching all 7 t values, constants}\"}, {\"[2,1,0]\", Column[T7`fitsAdj /. T7`tt -> tParam]}, {\"[3,1,0]\", Column[T7`fits310 /. T7`tt -> tParam]}, {\"[3,2,0]\", Column[T7`fits320 /. T7`tt -> tParam]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 7 addendum: t-dependence of the best locus of [3,2,0], the curve on which the columns (1,0) and (2,1) are decomposable together ({a gB = b gC^2, c gA = d gC}). Same driver, extra expression = saturated Groebner basis of the two columns' Pfaffians; then exact rational-function fits in t of gC/gA, gB/gA^2 and (gB + gA gC)/gA^2 (smallest degrees (m, n) of numerator/denominator through all 7 points). T7` symbols only (the driver wipes Global`). *)\nT7`curveExpr = \"Factor /@ GroebnerBasis[Append[DeleteCases[Union[Flatten[colPf @@@ {{1, 0}, {2, 1}}, 1]], 0], 1 - wSat gA gB gC], gVars, {wSat}]\";\nT7`runCurve[i_] := (T7`tmp = T7`run[\"{3, 2, 0}\", T7`pts[[i, 2]], T7`pts[[i, 3]], T7`pts[[i, 4]], T7`curveExpr]; {T7`pts[[i, 1]], T7`tmp[\"t\"], T7`tmp[\"extra\"]});\nT7`curve320 = T7`runCurve /@ {1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8};\nT7`ts = T7`curve320[[All, 2]];\nT7`ratios = Map[Function[row, {a1, b1} /. First[Solve[(row[[3]] /. {gA -> a1, gB -> b1, gC -> 1}) == 0, {a1, b1}]]], T7`curve320];   (* (gA/gC, gB/gC^2) at gC = 1 *)\nT7`ratFit[vals_] := Module[{res = {}}, Do[If[res === {} && m + n + 2 <= Length[T7`ts] - 1, Module[{p = Array[T7`pp, m + 1, 0], q = Array[T7`qq, n, 1], eqs, sol}, eqs = Table[(Sum[p[[k + 1]] T7`ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, m}]) - vals[[i]] (1 + Sum[q[[k]] T7`ts[[i]]^k, {k, 1, n}]) == 0, {i, Length[T7`ts]}]; sol = Quiet[Solve[eqs, Join[p, q]]]; If[sol =!= {}, res = {m, n, Factor[(Sum[p[[k + 1]] tParam^k, {k, 0, m}])/(1 + Sum[q[[k]] tParam^k, {k, 1, n}]) /. First[sol]]}]]], {tot, 0, 4}, {m, 0, tot}, {n, 0, tot - m}]; res];\nT7`gCgA = 1/T7`ratios[[All, 1]]; T7`gBgA2 = T7`ratios[[All, 2]]/T7`ratios[[All, 1]]^2;\nGrid[Join[Prepend[T7`curve320, {\"point\", \"t\", \"genuine ideal of the columns (1,0) and (2,1) of [3,2,0]\"}], {{\"fit gC/gA = (m, n, f(t))\", \"\", T7`ratFit[T7`gCgA]}, {\"fit gB/gA^2\", \"\", T7`ratFit[T7`gBgA2]}, {\"fit (gB + gA gC)/gA^2\", \"\", T7`ratFit[T7`gBgA2 + T7`gCgA]}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Not run in this session (scope reduced by Paul): the Task 7 driver cells of this section (the driver and the three rep runs, post-processing and the [3,2,0] curve addendum, i.e. the code cells after the Task 7 heading; they were cells 31-36 before section 6b was inserted). They wipe Global`, so they were left alone while section 6b was computed. The results below are those of the earlier session, kept as computed (that earlier session had already run them at all 8 points per rep, see the scope note inside).\n\n### Task 7 results (driver runs from this notebook's own file; 8 points per rep, 2.2 s ([2,1,0]) and about 14.5 s ([3,1,0], [3,2,0]) per point, 16 s / 114 s / 117 s per rep; the curve addendum of [3,2,0] 105 s)\n\n**Scope note (2026-10-10, later session).** Paul reduced the scope to [3,1,0] (3 points per rep: base, z', and h = 1/3 with theta = (1/5, -4/9)). The cells 32-36 had already been run at all 8 points for all three reps (including [3,2,0], cells 34 and 36) by the earlier session before the restriction arrived; those results are kept below as computed, and they contain the 3-point subset. No further [3,2,0] runs were made after the scope change.\n\n**z-independence (exact).** At z' = (3/2, 5/4, 3/7) (same h, theta) all K^(c2) matrices (exact rationals) and all column Pfaffian polynomials are **identical** to the base run for all three reps (printed flags {True, True}); so every locus of Tasks 4-5 is z-independent (K depends on (h, theta) only).\n\n**t-dependence.** The loci are hypersurfaces/curves whose coefficients depend on t = theta12/h only (checked: points with h = 1/3 agree with the h = 1/2 law). Conic constants cc (gB + gA gC = cc gA^2, i.e. b1 b3 = cc b2^2 on b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC)) per column and t (t = 62/35, 6/35, 16/15, 5/2, 7/3, 3/5, 29/15):\n\n| rep, column | cc at the 7 t values | Moebius fit cc(t) (exact on all 7) |\n|---|---|---|\n| [2,1,0] (1,0) | 43/16, 99/128, 29/28, -1/2, -1, 6/7, 8 | (t-3)/(2(t-2)) |\n| [3,1,0] (0,0), (1,0), (1,1) | 1 in all three columns at all 7 t | constant 1: **gB + gA gC = gA^2 (b2^2 = b1 b3), t-independent** |\n| [3,1,0] (1,1) | 39/4, 67/32, 22/7, -3, -5, 17/7, 31 | (t-4)/(t-2) |\n| [3,1,0] (1,0) | 52/43, 268/297, 88/87, 2, 5/3, 17/18, 31/24 | 2(t-4)/(3(t-3)) |\n| [3,1,0] (1,0) | 43/16, 99/128, 29/28, -1/2, -1, 6/7, 8 | (t-3)/(2(t-2)) (the adjoint quadric) |\n| [3,1,0] (1,0) | 1433/344, 12251/19008, 1291/1218, -3, -11/3, 97/126, 353/24 | not fitted by a (m/n) Moebius-type function with m + n <= 4 |\n| [3,2,0] (2,1) | 39/8, 67/64, 11/7, -3/2, -5/2, 17/14, 31/2 | (t-4)/(2(t-2)) |\n| [3,2,0] (2,0) | 13/2, 67/48, 44/21, -2, -10/3, 34/21, 62/3 | 2(t-4)/(3(t-2)) = (4/3) x the (2,1) constant |\n\n(The other factors, e.g. the gB-quadratic factor of [3,1,0] (0,0) and the non-conic factor of [3,2,0] (1,0), have t-dependent coefficients that were not analysed.) Best loci: [2,1,0]: 2(t-2)(gB + gA gC) = (t-3) gA^2 (reproduces the earlier adjoint law). [3,1,0]: gA^2 = gB + gA gC (no t at all; the two columns (0,0) and (1,1) share this factor, which is why they are decomposable together). [3,2,0] (1-dim curve for the columns (1,0) and (2,1)): ideals at the 7 t values {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC} (62/35), {67 gB = 18480 gC^2, 67 gA = 1120 gC} (6/35), {2816 gB = 9135 gC^2, 176 gA = 315 gC} (16/15), {25 gB = -4 gC^2, 5 gA = -4 gC} (5/2), {245 gB = -36 gC^2, 35 gA = -18 gC} (7/3), {17 gB = 280 gC^2, 17 gA = 70 gC} (3/5), {26071 gB = 1440 gC^2, 899 gA = 90 gC} (29/15). Exact fits through all 7 points (cell 36): gC/gA = t (t-4)/(6 (t-2)), gB/gA^2 = -(t-3)(t-4)/(6 (t-2)), hence (gB + gA gC)/gA^2 = (t-4)/(2(t-2)) = the conic constant of column (2,1): the curve lies on the conic of (2,1) and is cut out of it by a second t-dependent relation.\n\nNatural guess: the adjoint quadric constant (t-3)/(2(t-2)) generalises neither by the shift t -> t - k nor by a common factor: the new conic constants are (t-4)/(t-2), 2(t-4)/(3(t-3)), 1 ([3,1,0]) and (t-4)/(2(t-2)), 2(t-4)/(3(t-2)) ([3,2,0]), all with zeros/poles at the integers t = 2, 3, 4, the values of theta12/h at which a point theta1 - m1 h of the site-1 ladder coincides with a point theta2 - m2 h of the site-2 ladder (m1 - m2 = t).",
