   "value": "### site-1 rotation brackets, general reps — result (2026-10-10)\n\n**Label rule and wavefunction monomial (verified, all 3 reps, all 64/225/225 states, 3 (rows, k) conventions).** SoV labels (a|bc), lambda2 <= a <= lambda1, 0 <= c <= lambda2, c <= b <= a (count 8, 15, 15 = dim V); root triple theta_s + {-1-a, -b, -c} h; vacuum (lambda1|lambda1 lambda2) = triples (-3,-2,-1), (-4,-3,-1), (-4,-3,-2); x0 = e1 tensor e1 is the exact vacuum eigenvector of B. Wavefunction: psi_x/vac = N_x prod_s M^(s)_x/M^(s)_vac, M_(a|bc) = minor(n,n') v_k(theta - ch), (n,n') = (-1-a,-b), minor(n,n') = v_r1(n') v_r2(n) - v_r2(n') v_r1(n), valid for (rows, k) = ({1,2},1), ({2,3},3), ({1,3},2), deviation < 1e-43 / 1e-39 / 1e-40 (worst convention; others 1e-43 to 1e-46); N_x state independent; no shifted points needed.\n\n**Site-2 groups and factors.** The site-1 covectors tensor e1 occupy exactly the site-2 labels (lambda1|lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2 (2, 2, 3 groups; 12, 24, 28 SoV states; K ranks (4,8), (9,15), (4,9,15)), with factors lambda2^(c2) = v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) (k-independent to 1e-46: v(theta2 - c h) all parallel for c = 0..lambda2). K matrices exact rationals (denominators <= 6 digits).\n\n**Tensor supports (points m = -1-lambda1..0; columns c).** [2,1,0]: vacuum group {-3..0} (c=0), {-3,-2,-1} (c=1); group 0 {-3,-2,-1}, {-3,-2}. [3,1,0]: vacuum {-4..0}, {-4..-1}; group 0 {-4..-1}, {-4,-3,-2}. [3,2,0]: vacuum {-4..0}, {-4..-1}, {-4,-3,-2}; group 1 {-4..-1}, {-4,-3,-2}, {-4,-3}; group 0 {-4,-3,-2}, {-4,-3}, empty.\n\n**Automatic bracket counts (generic rotation = random covector):** 5, 7, 11 for [2,1,0], [3,1,0], [3,2,0] (per group: 2+3; 3+4; 2+4+5) vs dim V = 8, 15, 15 and |Lambda| = 3, 4, 5.\n\n**Loci (Gauss chart, exact).** [2,1,0]: only column (1,0) is non-automatic: {gB = 0} u {16(gB + gA gC) = 43 gA^2}; genuine = the quadric, dim 2; 43/16 = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) reproduced. [3,1,0]: non-automatic columns (0,0) [Pf = gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2)], (1,1) [(39 gA^2 - 4(gB + gA gC))(gA^2 - gB - gA gC)], (1,0) [five Pfaffians; genuine part EMPTY: the vacuum group is never fully decomposable by a genuine rotation, no (R2delta) analogue]. [3,2,0]: (1,0) [117 gA^2 gB - 86 gB^2 - 43 gA gB gC + 43 gA^2 gC^2 = 0, dim 2], (2,1) [39 gA^2 = 8(gB + gA gC), dim 2], (2,0) [genuine = curve {1247689 gB = 461332 gC^2, 1117 gA = -194 gC}, dim 1]; vacuum group jointly: EMPTY. Genuine rotations lie on every listed genuine component by construction (gA gB gC != 0).\n\n**Best reduced forms.** [2,1,0]: 4 brackets (generic 5) on the quadric (dim 2). [3,1,0]: **5** brackets (generic 7) on gA^2 = gB + gA gC (dim 2, b2^2 = b1 b3, no t dependence) and on the curve {243 gB = 280 gC^2, 351 gA = 140 gC}. [3,2,0]: **9** brackets (generic 11) only on the curve {12493 gB = 3010 gC^2, 403 gA = 140 gC}; every 2-dim locus gives 10. All verified against the exact overlap on all states: deviations < 1e-48, 1e-46, 1e-46 resp. (generic rotations < 1e-45, 1e-42, 1e-42).\n\n**Reach table (exact, finite twist).** Generic rotations and every genuine locus component (4 rational points each) reach all weights of V (7/7, 12/12, 12/12) with rank 2 on every doubly degenerate weight space, hence all required slice weights nu - Lambda of Lambda x Lambda (6, 10, 10 HW states): CG-complete at finite twist for all three reps and for the reduced loci.\n\n**z/t dependence.** z-independent (K, all Pfaffians identical at z'). t dependence: conic constants (t-3)/(2(t-2)) ([2,1,0]); 1, (t-4)/(t-2), 2(t-4)/(3(t-3)), (t-3)/(2(t-2)) ([3,1,0]); (t-4)/(2(t-2)), 2(t-4)/(3(t-2)) ([3,2,0]); the [3,2,0] best curve: gC/gA = t(t-4)/(6(t-2)), gB/gA^2 = -(t-3)(t-4)/(6(t-2)).\n\n**Timings.** Setup + SoV + wavefunction + K + tensors + loci + forms + reach per dim-15 rep: about 15 s in total (largest single steps: eigenvalue polynomials 2.7 s, dual Q's 1.1-1.3 s, B roots 1.6 s, wavefunction tests 1.5 s, symbolic tensors/Pfaffians a few s); Task 7 driver 16 s / 114 s / 117 s (+105 s curve addendum). No Groebner solve exceeded 1 s; no fallback was needed.\n\n**Structural surprises.** (1) For both dim-15 reps the vacuum group (the (R2delta) analogue) is NOT fully decomposable for any genuine rotation: [3,1,0] its 5-point column (1,0) has an empty genuine Pfaffian locus (dim 1 of degenerate points only); [3,2,0] its columns (2,0) (a curve) and (2,1) (a conic surface) are incompatible. The decomposability is available only for non-vacuum-group columns, and then for [3,1,0] on a 2-dim family, for [3,2,0] only on a 1-dim family. (2) The adjoint quadric constant (t-3)/(2(t-2)) occurs again in [3,1,0] (column (1,0)) but only as one factor of one Pfaffian. (3) [3,1,0] has a t-independent factor gB + gA gC = gA^2 shared by columns (0,0), (1,0), (1,1) (the natural 2-dim family). (4) Group c2 = 0 of [3,2,0] has an identically zero column c = 2 and its columns c = 0, 1 are always decomposable; the counts per group are 2, 4, 5. (5) VS Code did not open the new notebook: no native outputs; results are in the markdown cells.\n\n**Closed-form bracket measures (section 6b, added later the same day; exact, symbolic in the two free parameters (gA, gC) = (alpha, gamma) of the loci).** Gauge: pivot (i,j) of the column 2-form A, F = A[All,i]/A_ij, G = A[All,j] (so A = F^G with (F^G)_{ab} = F_a G_b - F_b G_a), F_i = 0, F_j = -1, G_j = 0; pivots restricted to A_ij that are products of gA, gC and (gA - gC) (= beta/alpha) so that F, G have poles only on alpha beta gamma = 0. Points m = -4..0 ([3,1,0]) resp. m = -3..0 ([2,1,0]); (c2, c) = (group, column), c2 = 1 the vacuum group.\n\n[3,1,0] on beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (gB = gA^2 - gA gC; b = (1, alpha, alpha^2)), t = 62/35, **5 wedges**:\n- (0,0), pivot (1,4): `F = {0, (31*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(12*gA^2*(gA - gC)), (124*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(81*gA*(gA - gC)), -1, 0}`, `G = {(-105*gA^3*(gA - gC))/62, (4515*gA^4*(gA - gC))/248, (1505*gA^5*(gA - gC))/558, 0, 0}`\n- (0,1), pivot (1,2): `F = {0, -1, (-4*gA)/9, 0, 0}`, `G = {(3395*gA)/248, 0, (145985*gA^3)/3348, 0, 0}`\n- (1,0) (vacuum, rank 4: two wedges), pivot (1,5): `F = {0, -1/43*(27*gA - 62*gC)/(gA^3*(gA - gC)), (58*gA - 93*gC)/(4*gA^2*(gA - gC)), (62*(2*gA - 3*gC))/(27*gA*(gA - gC)), -1}`, `G = {(43*gA^3*(gA - gC))/62, (-129*gA^4*(gA - gC))/62, (129*gA^5*(gA - gC))/62, 0, 0}`; then pivot (2,4): `F = {0, 0, 0, -1, 0}`, `G = {0, gA^3*(gA - gC), (-129*gA^4*(gA - gC))/8, 0, 0}`\n- (1,1), pivot (1,2): `F = {0, -1, (129*gA)/8, (43*gA^2)/9, 0}`, `G = {1, 0, -41*gA^2, (-344*gA^3)/27, 0}`\n\n[2,1,0] on 16 (beta + alpha gamma) = 43 alpha^2 (gB = 43 gA^2/16 - gA gC), t = 62/35, **4 wedges**:\n- (0,0), pivot (1,3): `F = {0, (31*(43*gA - 32*gC))/(27*gA*(43*gA - 16*gC)), -1, 0}`, `G = {(35*gA^2*(43*gA - 16*gC))/496, (1505*gA^3*(43*gA - 16*gC))/26784, 0, 0}`\n- (0,1), pivot (1,2): `F = {0, -1, 0, 0}`, `G = {(-3395*gA)/1674, 0, 0, 0}`\n- (1,0) (vacuum), pivot (1,4): `F = {0, (2*(27*gA - 62*gC))/(gA^2*(43*gA - 16*gC)), (62*(43*gA - 32*gC))/(27*gA*(43*gA - 16*gC)), -1}`, `G = {-1/124*(gA^2*(43*gA - 16*gC)), (43*gA^3*(43*gA - 16*gC))/992, 0, 0}`\n- (1,1), pivot (1,2): `F = {0, -1, (-16*gA)/27, 0}`, `G = {1, 0, (43*gA^2)/18, 0}`\n\nVerification: sum of wedges = column, symbolic residual 0 for all (c2, c) of both reps; at the Task 5 points the wedge sums equal the Task 5 ones exactly; full overlap identity on all 225 / 64 states at two fresh rational points of each locus and at the Task 5 point: deviation < 3e-46 ([3,1,0]) and < 2e-48 ([2,1,0]) (bigfloat zeros). Structure: the c = 1 columns ((0,1), (1,1)) depend on gA only; delta-function measures: [3,1,0] only F of the second wedge of the vacuum column (F = -delta_{m=-1}); [2,1,0] column (0,1) = product of two deltas; zero slots (n,0) for the c = 1 columns and for group-0 column (0,0); all entries Laurent monomials in gA times one linear factor over (gA - gC); **no gauge makes F or G independent of (gA, gC) for [3,1,0]; for [2,1,0] only the column (0,1) (constant plane span{e_-3, e_-2})**. Natural measure wgt(m) rho^m (p + q m) on the column support: yes with rational rho only for supports of at most 3 points ([3,1,0] (0,1) F: rho = -4 gA/9, p = -64 gA^3/729, q = -16 gA^3/729; [2,1,0] (0,0) F: rho = 27 gA (43 gA - 16 gC)/(31 (43 gA - 32 gC)), (0,0) G: rho = -43 gA/54, (1,1) F: rho = -16 gA/27; complex rho = +- i sqrt(86/27) gA resp. +- (i/3) sqrt(43/2) gA for G of [3,1,0] (0,1) resp. [2,1,0] (1,1)); **no** for every vector on the 4- and 5-point columns ((0,0), (1,0), (1,1) of [3,1,0]; (1,0) of [2,1,0]), the planes only contain natural vectors for roots of irreducible quartics/cubics.\n\nt-dependence (6b-5/6b-6, 10 values of t, exact): the locus gB + gA gC = gA^2 is t-independent (residual 0 at all 10 t; at t = 29/15 the Pfaffians are (0,0): (5400/203) gB (gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(3 gA^2 gB - gB^2 + gA gB gC + 2 gA^2 gC^2), (1,1): (-48/7)(gA^2 - gB - gA gC)(31 gA^2 - gB - gA gC); the genuine part of the vacuum column (1,0) stays empty at every t), and every F, G coefficient is a short rational function of t with poles only at t in {0, 1, 2, 3}: (0,0) F = {0, -t(2gA-3gC)/(3(t-2)gA^2(gA-gC)), 2t(2gA-3gC)/(3(t-1)gA(gA-gC)), -1, 0}, G = {-3gA^3(gA-gC)/t, 6(t-3)gA^4(gA-gC)/(t(t-2)), -3(t-3)gA^5(gA-gC)/(t(t-1)), 0, 0}; (0,1) F = {0, -1, 3(t-2)gA/(2(t-1)), 0, 0}, G = {-2(t+1)gA/(t(t-2)), 0, 4(t-3)(t+1)gA^3/(t(t-1)(t-2)), 0, 0}; (1,0) wedge 1 F = {0, ((t-1)gA - t gC)/((t-3)gA^3(gA-gC)), -((3t-2)gA - 3t gC)/((t-2)gA^2(gA-gC)), t(2gA-3gC)/((t-1)gA(gA-gC)), -1}, G = {-(t-3)gA^3(gA-gC)/t, 3(t-3)gA^4(gA-gC)/t, -3(t-3)gA^5(gA-gC)/t, 0, 0}, wedge 2 F = {0,0,0,-1,0}, G = {0, gA^3(gA-gC), -3(t-3)gA^4(gA-gC)/(t-2), 0, 0}; (1,1) F = {0, -1, 3(t-3)gA/(t-2), -3(t-3)gA^2/(t-1), 0}, G = {1, 0, -2(3t-10)gA^2/(t-2), 8(t-3)gA^3/(t-1), 0}. [The Task 7 driver cells 31-36 were NOT re-run in this session (scope reduced by Paul); the z-independence and the other-rep t-laws quoted above are from the earlier session. [3,2,0] was not extended with closed forms.]\n\n**Timings of section 6b.** Setup for a rep (cells 3-6, 9-10, 13, 16, 19): 7.6 s ([3,1,0], fresh kernel; up to 18 s in a busy one), 0.9 s ([2,1,0]); closed-form decomposition 0.07 s, verification 0.33 s (225 states, 3 points), structure and natural-measure cells 0.05 s each; the 10-point t-driver cell 142 s (about 14 s per point) plus the fit 0.2 s. **Surprises of 6b:** the cheapest pivot is singular at the Task 5 rational point (hence the pivot rule); the first natural-measure test counted rho = 0 as a common root (fixed); one sampled (h, theta) point (theta2 = 3/4) stalled the setup for more than 100 s; the cell-37 \"placeholder\" actually holds the earlier session's Task 7 results (kept, with a note).\n\n**u-structure of the bracket measures of [3,1,0] (section 6c, 2026-10-10, later session).** The gauge-invariant column kernel A^(c2,c) = sum of F^G over the wedges is A_{mm'} = gA^(m+m'+9-c2-c) a_{mm'}(s, t), s = gC/gA: the gA-dependence is a pure exponential gA^((u+u'-2 theta1)/h) with a column-dependent constant 9, 8, 8, 7 for (0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1) (adjoint: 7, 6, 6, 5), and the residual kernels are affine in s with poles only at t in {0, 1, 2} (exact, verified against direct tensors at t = 62/35 and at h = 1/3, t = 29/15). Nice-basis tests (classes: wgt5, global eight-pole wgt8, no measure, cross-ladder poles; polynomial degree <= 2 in u; exact generic dimension of P cap class): **no column is natural in any of these classes** (rank-2 columns: dimension 0 for all; the rank-4 vacuum column (1,0) cannot lie in a class of dimension <= 3). Positive structure: (0,1) (3-point support) is wgt3 Pol_1/(m (t+m+1)): F(u) = h^4 gA^((u-theta1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-theta1)(u-theta2+h)), G(u) = h^3 gA^((u-theta1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-theta2+h)), A^(0,1) = 48 (t-3)(t+1)/t gA^8 F^G; (0,0) (support {-4..-1}) is wgt4 Pol_1/(t+m+1) up to ONE end-point rescaling at m = -1 by 3(s-1)/(3s-2); (1,1) is the t-linear pencil (t-3) D v^(t x + y) D with the t-independent common vector v = -6 w1(m) (ladder-1 four-pole measure truncated at m = 0) but is NOT of the form wgt4 Pol_1/nu for any nu (Moebius determinant -24 (t-1)(t-2)(t-3)); (1,0) contains delta_{-1} and one vector on every pair of points, no class. The u-function forms of (0,1) and (0,0) reproduce the full overlap on all 225 states to below 10^-45.",
